    <node id="Questions to Ask">
      <data key="d0">Questions to Ask</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Questions to Ask is a recurring section found at the end of each chapter in the NCCN Guidelines for Patients, as well as in the associated book format of these guidelines. This section is designed to provide a curated list of suggested questions that patients can use to facilitate more informed discussions with their healthcare providers. The primary purpose of this feature is to empower patients by helping them gather more detailed information about their condition, treatment options, and care plan. By offering these targeted questions, the section aims to support patients in actively engaging with their care team, ensuring they can clarify uncertainties and make more educated decisions about their health journey.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-058&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-067&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-068&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-075&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-169</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682788</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="General Health Tests">
      <data key="d0">General Health Tests</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">General Health Tests are a category of medical evaluations designed to assess an individual's overall health status. These tests are often part of the diagnostic process for conditions such as basal cell skin cancer, where they help establish a baseline of the patient's general well-being. The scope of these tests is broad, typically encompassing a review of the patient's medical history, family history, and lifestyle factors, including tobacco and alcohol use. A physical examination is also a standard component of this assessment.

The composition of General Health Tests can vary, ranging from a basic set that includes a medical history review and physical exam to a more comprehensive suite that adds family history and other assessments. In some cases, these tests are described as routine procedures that include objective measurements like blood tests and vital sign checks. Regardless of the specific combination, the primary purpose remains consistent: to provide a holistic evaluation of a patient's health, which can inform further diagnostic or preventive care decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-075&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-096&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-098&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-127&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-154&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-172</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
