    <node id="Medical Binder">
      <data key="d0">Medical Binder</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A Medical Binder is a physical notebook or binder designed to organize a patient's medical information in a centralized and accessible manner. Its primary purpose is to compile and store copies of essential medical records, including blood tests, imaging results, and various medical reports. The binder serves as a practical tool for managing healthcare documentation, ensuring that patients or caregivers can easily locate and present their medical history when needed.

The structure of a Medical Binder is often customizable to enhance organization. It may include dedicated folders or dividers for different categories of documents, such as insurance forms, specific test types, treatments, and procedures. Additionally, the binder frequently features a designated section for recording questions and personal notes, allowing users to track concerns or instructions during medical appointments. By consolidating these materials, the Medical Binder functions as a comprehensive and portable health record system, supporting better communication between patients and healthcare providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-054&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-100&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-101</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682803</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Primary Care Physician">
      <data key="d0">Primary Care Physician</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Primary Care Physician is a doctor or physician who provides general medical care and serves as a foundational figure in a patient's healthcare journey. This professional is often the first point of contact for patients experiencing new symptoms, such as rectal bleeding, and may refer them to appropriate specialists for further evaluation and treatment. The Primary Care Physician is responsible for coordinating care with these specialists, ensuring a cohesive approach to the patient's overall health.

A key responsibility of the Primary Care Physician is staying informed about the patient's condition and any changes in their health status. This includes being updated on significant developments, such as a cancer diagnosis and the details of the patient's cancer care. The physician is also expected to be kept abreast of any modifications to the patient's broader care team, including changes to the team's contact list. This ensures that the Primary Care Physician can effectively communicate and collaborate with all other healthcare providers involved in the patient's treatment. In some cases, the Primary Care Physician may also be an active part of the cancer care team itself.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-064&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-095&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-127&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-136&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-161&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-163&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-173&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-178&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-186</data>
