    </node>
    <node id="Vitamin D">
      <data key="d0">Vitamin D</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">A nutrient that calcipotriene is a form of, which activates the skin's immune system.&lt;SEP&gt;A vitamin supplement recommended to help strengthen bones during thyroid cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-148</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tirbanibulin">
      <data key="d0">Tirbanibulin</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A topical microtubule inhibitor used to treat actinic keratosis on the face or scalp, applied once daily for five consecutive days.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hyperkeratosis">
      <data key="d0">Hyperkeratosis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Thickening of the outer layer of skin, often associated with actinic keratoses.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tazarotene">
      <data key="d0">Tazarotene</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A retinoid product related to vitamin A, used topically for hyperkeratotic actinic keratoses.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Curettage">
      <data key="d0">Curettage</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Scraping away skin with a spoon-shaped tool, often used before other treatments for actinic keratoses.&lt;SEP&gt;A surgical procedure that uses a curette to scrape away cancer cells, often used in combination with electrodesiccation.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-012</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Topical Keratolytics">
      <data key="d0">Topical Keratolytics</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Topical agents such as urea, lactic acid, or salicylic acid used to soften and break down thick skin.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Topical Diclofenac">
      <data key="d0">Topical Diclofenac</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A topical therapy sometimes used for actinic keratoses.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chemical Peels">
      <data key="d0">Chemical Peels</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A treatment using trichloroacetic acid for actinic keratoses.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Resurfacing Techniques">
      <data key="d0">Resurfacing Techniques</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Techniques such as laser or dermabrasion used for actinic keratoses.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mohs Surgery">
      <data key="d0">Mohs Surgery</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A surgical procedure that removes skin cancer layer by layer, examining each layer for cancer cells until none remain.&lt;SEP&gt;A surgical technique that removes skin cancer layer by layer, examining each layer for cancer cells, used for high-risk and very high-risk CSCC.&lt;SEP&gt;A specialized surgical technique that removes skin cancer layer by layer, examining each layer for cancer cells until no cancer remains, used for certain types of CSCC.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-013</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Curettage and Electrodesiccation">
      <data key="d0">Curettage and Electrodesiccation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A two-step procedure scraping off the tumor and then cauterizing the base with an electric needle, used for early CSCC.&lt;SEP&gt;A surgical treatment option for low-risk, local CSCC, involving scraping and burning the tumor.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-012</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PDEMA">
      <data key="d0">PDEMA</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Peripheral and deep en face margin assessment, a type of surgery that allows complete testing of edges of removed tissue, often used on head, face, hands, feet, shins, and genital areas.&lt;SEP&gt;A form of peripheral deep excision with margin assessment, similar to Mohs surgery, used for high-risk CSCC.&lt;SEP&gt;A form of surgical excision that may be used as an alternative to Mohs surgery for certain skin cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-013</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Standard Surgical Excision">
      <data key="d0">Standard Surgical Excision</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A surgical procedure removing the tumor and a margin of normal tissue, with edges sent for pathological examination.&lt;SEP&gt;A surgical procedure to remove the tumor along with some surrounding healthy tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;A surgical treatment option for CSCC, removing the tumor with a margin of normal tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;A surgical procedure to remove a skin cancer lesion along with a margin of normal tissue, recommended for high-risk or very high-risk local CSCC.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-013</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lymph Node Dissection">
      <data key="d0">Lymph Node Dissection</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A more extensive surgery to remove lymph nodes if biopsy shows cancer, usually under general anesthesia.&lt;SEP&gt;Surgical removal of lymph nodes to test for cancer, also called lymphadenectomy.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-138</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sentinel Lymph Node Biopsy">
      <data key="d0">Sentinel Lymph Node Biopsy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A surgery to remove and examine sentinel lymph nodes for cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A surgical procedure that removes tissue samples to examine sentinel lymph nodes for cancer cells, used for staging and treatment planning.&lt;SEP&gt;A procedure to identify and remove the first lymph nodes where cancer might have spread, using dye and radioactive solution.&lt;SEP&gt;A procedure to remove sentinel lymph nodes during surgery to determine if cancer cells have traveled to the lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;A procedure to remove sentinel lymph nodes to check for cancer spread.&lt;SEP&gt;Procedure to identify and remove sentinel lymph nodes most likely to contain cancer using dye or radioactive substance.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-104&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-109&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-138</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dermatologic Surgeon">
      <data key="d0">Dermatologic Surgeon</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A skin surgeon with special training in procedures like Mohs surgery.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="General Anesthesia">
      <data key="d0">General Anesthesia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A state of deep sleep induced for more extensive surgeries like lymph node dissection.&lt;SEP&gt;A state of deep sleep induced for surgery, mentioned as used for extensive surgery and sentinel lymph node biopsy.&lt;SEP&gt;Medicine given to put a patient into a deep sleep to prevent pain during surgery.&lt;SEP&gt;A state of controlled unconsciousness induced for medical procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical state induced to prevent pain during procedures, often required for brachytherapy applicator placement.&lt;SEP&gt;A state of controlled unconsciousness induced for surgical procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Sometimes used during high-resolution anoscopy when performed in the operating room.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-135&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-139&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-147&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-186</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Surgical Margin">
      <data key="d0">Surgical Margin</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The edges of removed tissue during standard surgical excision, examined for cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;The area of normal tissue around a tumor that is removed during surgery to ensure complete removal.&lt;SEP&gt;The normal tissue surrounding a removed lesion; a margin of at least 1 cm without cancer cells is desired.&lt;SEP&gt;The normal tissue surrounding the lesion removed during surgery.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-190&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-191</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Scalpel">
      <data key="d0">Scalpel</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A surgical instrument used to remove tumors and tissue layers in procedures like Mohs surgery and standard excision.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Electric Needle">
      <data key="d0">Electric Needle</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A tool used in curettage and electrodesiccation to cauterize the base of the wound.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Microscope">
      <data key="d0">Microscope</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">An instrument used by surgeons and pathologists to examine tissue for cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;An instrument used to study cells after staining in IHC.&lt;SEP&gt;An instrument used by pathologists to examine cells and tissue for abnormalities.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-105&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-176</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Secondary Intention Healing">
      <data key="d0">Secondary Intention Healing</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A wound healing process where a wound is left open to heal naturally, filling in and closing up without stitches.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Linear Closure">
      <data key="d0">Linear Closure</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A wound closure technique where the surgeon reshapes the wound into a fusiform shape and stitches it in a line.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Skin Graft">
      <data key="d0">Skin Graft</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A surgical procedure where a patch of skin is removed from one area and transplanted to another to aid healing and reduce scarring.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="External Beam Radiation Therapy">
      <data key="d0">External Beam Radiation Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of radiation therapy where a beam of radiation is directed at the tumor from a machine, using electrons or photons.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of radiation therapy that uses external beams to treat cancer, which can damage ovaries.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of radiation therapy that uses a machine outside the body to aim radiation at the whole breast and lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Radiation therapy using a machine to aim radiation at the cancer site.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-060&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-110&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-138</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Brachytherapy">
      <data key="d0">Brachytherapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of radiation therapy where a radiation source is placed close to or in direct contact with the tumor for a short time.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of radiation therapy where radioactive material is placed inside or near the tumor.&lt;SEP&gt;Internal radiation therapy that involves placing radioactive material inside the body to target tumors while limiting radiation to surrounding tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;Treatment with radioactive material placed inside the body to deliver a high dose of radiation directly to the tumor.&lt;SEP&gt;Internal radiation therapy where radioactive material is placed near the tumor.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of radiation therapy where radioactive material is placed inside or near the tumor, used as a treatment option for local recurrence.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-137&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-139&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-140&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-142&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-143&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-144</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Adjuvant Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Adjuvant Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Therapy given after primary treatment to lower the risk of cancer recurrence, often using radiation after surgery.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic treatment given after surgery.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-110</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682867</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lymphocytes">
      <data key="d0">Lymphocytes</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lymphocytes are a type of white blood cell that forms a crucial part of the immune system, helping to fight and prevent infection and disease. They are found in the blood, lymph tissue, and throughout all organs of the body. There are three main types of lymphocytes: B lymphocytes (B cells), T lymphocytes (T cells), and natural killer cells. Lymphocytes develop from lymphoid progenitor cells and mature from lymphoblasts.

These cells are central to immune function and are also key to understanding several diseases. Lymphocytes can grow out of control and become cancerous, leading to conditions such as lymphoma, including Hodgkin lymphoma. Additionally, acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) originates in lymphocytes, as this cancer starts in these white blood cells. The abnormal overgrowth of lymphocytes is directly linked to the development of lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-058&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-065&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-074&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-075&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-112&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-113&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-171&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-172</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682869</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d0">Chemotherapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Chemotherapy is a cancer treatment modality that uses drugs to kill cancer cells, typically by targeting fast-dividing or rapidly growing cells. As a systemic therapy, it works throughout the body, with drugs traveling via the bloodstream to reach cells in various locations. It is often administered intravenously, either as an infusion or injection, but can also be given orally, intraperitoneally, or directly into the bladder, depending on the cancer type. Chemotherapy is frequently delivered in cycles, allowing the body time to recover between treatments. It can be used as a primary treatment, a standard of care for certain cancers like acute myeloid leukemia (AML), primary CNS lymphoma, and high-grade gliomas, or as part of a combined approach with other therapies, such as radiation (chemoradiation) or immune checkpoint inhibitors.

The application of chemotherapy varies by cancer type and stage. It may be given before surgery (neoadjuvant) to shrink tumors, after surgery (adjuvant) based on disease stage, or as the main treatment for advanced or metastatic cancers, including ovarian, anal, prostate, and perianal cancers. For certain conditions, such as mediastinal gray zone lymphoma or anaplastic thyroid cancer, it is a common or necessary treatment, though it is not highly effective against most thyroid cancers. In stem cell rescue procedures, high-dose chemotherapy is used to destroy lymphoma cells and bone marrow stem cells. Specific drug examples include platinum-based agents like cisplatin and carboplatin, as well as capecitabine and paclitaxel.

Because chemotherapy targets all fast-dividing cells, it can also harm healthy cells, leading to side effects such as nausea, vomiting, fatigue, diarrhea, hair loss, mouth sores, fever, infection, tingling or numbness, and rash. Long-term side effects may include other cancers, heart disease, and infertility, as the treatment can affect fertility. Chemotherapy is considered a non-hormone therapy and is a cornerstone of systemic cancer treatment, though its effectiveness and side effects depend on the specific drugs used and the individual patient's condition.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-062&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-072&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-073&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-081&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-093&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-101&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-105&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-109&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-110&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-111&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-113&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-116&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-117&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-118&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-119&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-120&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-122&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-124&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-125&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-128&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-130&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-138&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-139&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-146&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-149&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-164&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-165&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-168&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-175&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-176&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-180&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-182&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-183&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-184&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-185&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-188&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-189&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-190&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-191&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-192&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-193&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-194&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-196</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
