    </node>
    <node id="Cisplatin">
      <data key="d0">Cisplatin</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Cisplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug used in the treatment of various cancers, including squamous cell skin cancer, cervical cancer, bladder cancer, and anal cancer. It is administered intravenously and is often combined with other medications, such as 5-FU for anal or perianal cancer, and is generally preferred for cervical cancer, where it is given weekly during chemoradiation or every three weeks for recurrent or metastatic cases. In some instances, it is used alongside other medicines if prior treatment has been received.

Cisplatin is effective but carries a range of potential side effects, including mouth sores, hair loss, fatigue, increased risk of infection, easy bleeding or bruising, nerve damage, kidney damage, tinnitus, and hearing problems. With extended or repeat use, it can cause kidney damage and hearing issues, and it may also trigger hypersensitivity reactions upon repeated administration.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-139&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-140&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-144&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-145&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-183&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-190&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-191&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-192&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-193&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-194</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682874</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Carboplatin">
      <data key="d0">Carboplatin</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Carboplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug utilized in systemic therapy for the treatment of various malignancies. It is primarily indicated for squamous cell skin cancer and is a standard component in regimens for ovarian cancer. Additionally, it is used in combination with paclitaxel for the treatment of anal cancer. Carboplatin is frequently employed as a therapeutic alternative to cisplatin, particularly in cases where cisplatin is considered too harsh or cannot be administered due to patient intolerance or contraindications. A notable adverse effect associated with carboplatin is the potential to cause hypersensitivity reactions, which may occur with repeated use of the drug.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-109&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-139&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-145&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-192&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-193</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682875</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Basal Cell Nevus Syndrome">
      <data key="d0">Basal Cell Nevus Syndrome</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A genetic condition that increases the risk of skin cancer caused by radiation, making radiation therapy inappropriate.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682875</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lupus">
      <data key="d0">Lupus</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A connective tissue disease that may make radiation therapy inappropriate for some patients.&lt;SEP&gt;An autoimmune disease that may increase the risk of primary CNS lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-112</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682875</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Scleroderma">
      <data key="d0">Scleroderma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A connective tissue disease that may make radiation therapy inappropriate for some patients.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682875</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sentinel Lymph Node">
      <data key="d0">Sentinel Lymph Node</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The first lymph node to which cancer cells most likely spread from a primary tumor; there can be more than one.&lt;SEP&gt;The first lymph node that cancer cells are most likely to spread to from a primary tumor.&lt;SEP&gt;The first lymph node that cancer cells are most likely to spread to from a primary tumor. There can be more than one sentinel lymph node.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-103&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-104</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682875</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Wound Healing">
      <data key="d0">Wound Healing</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The process by which the skin repairs itself after surgery, with methods including secondary intention and linear closure.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of healing wounds, which can be impaired by smoking and vaping.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682875</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Skin Grafting">
      <data key="d0">Skin Grafting</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A surgical technique involving transplanting skin from one area to another to promote healing and reduce scarring.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682875</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Flapping">
      <data key="d0">Flapping</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A surgical technique that rearranges skin to help wounds heal and lessen scarring.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682875</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Electrons">
      <data key="d0">Electrons</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of radiation used in external beam radiation therapy to treat superficial tumors.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682875</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Photons">
      <data key="d0">Photons</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">High-energy x-rays used in external beam radiation therapy to treat deeper, more invasive tumors.&lt;SEP&gt;Particles of light used in radiation therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-109</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682875</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Protons">
      <data key="d0">Protons</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Charged particles used in radiation therapy to kill cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Positively charged particles used in radiation therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-109</data>
