    <node id="Immunotherapy">
      <data key="d0">Immunotherapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Immunotherapy is a form of cancer treatment that leverages the body's own immune system to identify, target, and destroy cancer cells. It is classified as a systemic therapy, meaning it works throughout the body, and functions by either stimulating or re-activating the immune system's natural defenses against tumors. This approach can be administered alone or in combination with other treatments, and its application spans various cancer types, including recurrent ovarian cancer, advanced-stage prostate cancer, recurrent or metastatic cervical cancer, metastatic thyroid cancer, and primary CNS lymphoma, where the monoclonal antibody rituximab is a key agent.

A prominent and often preferred method within immunotherapy involves the use of immune checkpoint inhibitors, which include drugs that target proteins such as PD-1 and PD-L1. A specific example of this class is pembrolizumab. These inhibitors are frequently utilized in clinical practice, particularly for cancers like metastatic anal cancer, where they serve as a primary treatment or are recommended when the disease progresses during or after chemotherapy. In some cases, such as progressive anal cancer, these inhibitors may be administered before surgery. Additionally, immunotherapy can be delivered directly into the bladder for certain malignancies.

The application of immunotherapy is sometimes guided by the presence of specific biomarkers to determine patient eligibility. While it offers a powerful mechanism for fighting cancer, it is not without side effects. Potential adverse reactions include autoimmune responses, fatigue, fever, nausea, loss of appetite, infection, diarrhea, and constipation. Overall, immunotherapy represents a versatile and increasingly central strategy in oncology, offering options for both early and advanced-stage diseases across a wide spectrum of cancer types.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-073&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-093&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-109&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-111&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-116&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-119&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-120&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-125&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-130&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-139&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-140&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-143&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-144&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-145&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-149&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-152&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-153&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-175&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-176&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-180&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-182&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-183&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-184&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-188&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-189&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-191&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chun