    <node id="Informed Consent">
      <data key="d0">Informed Consent</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A process in clinical trials where the research team reviews the study details, risks, and benefits with participants, who sign an informed consent form.&lt;SEP&gt;A process and form that provides detailed information about a clinical trial, including purpose, risks, and benefits.&lt;SEP&gt;A process where the research team reviews the study details, risks, and benefits with participants, and participants sign an informed consent form.&lt;SEP&gt;A process in clinical trials where the research team reviews the study details, including purpose, risks, and benefits, with the participant. Information is provided in an informed consent form, which must be read and signed before participation.&lt;SEP&gt;An agreement confirming that a participant has been fully informed about the trial, including its purpose, risks, and benefits.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-117&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-140&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-149&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-184</data>
