    <node id="Placebo">
      <data key="d0">Placebo</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An inactive version of a real medicine, almost never used alone in cancer clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;An inactive substance or treatment that looks like the real medicine but has no therapeutic effect.&lt;SEP&gt;An inactive version of a real medicine. Placebos are almost never used alone in cancer clinical trials; they may be given with a standard treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;An inactive substance or treatment used as a control in clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;An inactive substance used in clinical trials as a control, which participants are informed about before enrollment.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-117&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-140&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-149&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-150&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-184&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-193&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-194</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682884</data>
