    <node id="Standard Treatment">
      <data key="d0">Standard Treatment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The usual or established treatment for a condition, as opposed to an experimental treatment in a clinical trial.&lt;SEP&gt;The usual or established treatment for a condition, used as a comparison in clinical trials.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-184</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Study Sponsor">
      <data key="d0">Study Sponsor</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The organization or entity that funds and oversees a clinical trial, responsible for research-related costs.&lt;SEP&gt;The entity that funds and oversees a clinical trial, covering research-related costs.&lt;SEP&gt;The entity that pays for research-related costs in a clinical trial, including the study drug.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-150&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-193&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-194</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Insurance">
      <data key="d0">Insurance</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A financial arrangement that covers medical costs, often used to pay for standard cancer care during a trial.&lt;SEP&gt;A system for covering medical costs, often used to pay for standard cancer care during trials.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial coverage for medical tests and treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;Health insurance that often covers standard treatment costs in clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;Coverage that often pays for standard cancer care during a trial, with patients responsible for copays and uncovered costs.&lt;SEP&gt;Health coverage concerns that may affect cancer survivors.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-150&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-157&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-184&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-194&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-196</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Copay">
      <data key="d0">Copay</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A fixed amount a patient pays for a covered healthcare service, as required by their insurance.&lt;SEP&gt;A fixed amount a patient pays for covered health care services, as mentioned in trial costs.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-184</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Transportation Cost">
      <data key="d0">Transportation Cost</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Expenses related to traveling to and from medical appointments, which may be indirectly related to a clinical trial.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Child Care Cost">
      <data key="d0">Child Care Cost</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Expenses for caring for children while a patient attends medical appointments, which may be indirectly related to a clinical trial.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Local Recurrence">
      <data key="d0">Local Recurrence</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The return of cancer in the same area where it originally started.&lt;SEP&gt;A cancer recurrence that occurs in the same area as the original tumor, often treated with surgery and radiation.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-144</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tumor Border">
      <data key="d0">Tumor Border</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The edge or boundary of a tumor, which can be well-defined or uneven, affecting risk assessment.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Damaged Skin">
      <data key="d0">Damaged Skin</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Skin that has been previously treated with radiation, or has wounds, scars, or inflammation, which can increase cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nerve Damage">
      <data key="d0">Nerve Damage</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Injury to nerves, which can be a sign of perineural invasion in cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A side effect of chemotherapy, also known as neuropathy, can be more severe with intraperitoneal chemotherapy.&lt;SEP&gt;A potential side effect of extended treatment with oxaliplatin, affecting fingers and toes.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-193</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tumor Cells">
      <data key="d0">Tumor Cells</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Abnormal cells that divide and grow uncontrollably, forming a tumor.&lt;SEP&gt;Cells that can be killed by T cells and natural killer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Abnormal cells that form tumors, whose appearance under a microscope determines grade.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-065&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-159&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-069</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Normal Cells">
      <data key="d0">Normal Cells</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Healthy cells that function normally and have a typical appearance under a microscope.&lt;SEP&gt;Cells that behave according to normal growth and function rules, which are overwhelmed by cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;PCR can find 1 abnormal cell among more than 100,000 normal cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Cells that behave normally and are replaced by cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Cells that behave in a regulated manner, unlike cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Cells that follow the body's rules, increasing only when needed and dying when old or damaged.&lt;SEP&gt;Healthy cells that behave according to genetic instructions.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-095&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-164&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-174</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
