    <node id="Tumor Type">
      <data key="d0">Tumor Type</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The specific type and subtype of squamous cell skin cancer determined by a pathologist from a biopsy.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-012</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Treatment Team">
      <data key="d0">Treatment Team</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Treatment Team is a group of healthcare professionals involved in a patient's cancer care, responsible for providing comprehensive care and guidance. This team typically includes doctors, nurses, and specialists, such as urologists, who collaborate to manage the patient's condition. Their primary duties involve working with the patient to determine the most appropriate therapies for their specific cancer type, following established best practices. The team also plays a key role in recommending and conducting biomarker testing, using biopsy results to inform treatment planning, and deciding on suitable therapeutic approaches. Additionally, they are tasked with managing the patient's cancer treatment and associated side effects, while providing essential information on these topics to ensure the patient is well-informed throughout their care journey.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-089&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-104&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-105&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-119&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-167&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-174&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-185&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-196</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682894</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lymphovascular Invasion">
      <data key="d0">Lymphovascular Invasion</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The presence of cancer cells in blood or lymph vessels outside the main tumor, indicating a higher risk of spread.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-012</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682894</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Low-risk CSCC">
      <data key="d0">Low-risk CSCC</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A category of squamous cell skin cancer that has not spread to lymph nodes and is treated with surgery or radiation.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-012</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682894</data>
