    <node id="Chromosome 9">
      <data key="d0">Chromosome 9</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">A chromosome that breaks off and trades places with a piece of chromosome 22 in CML.&lt;SEP&gt;A chromosome that breaks off and switches places with a piece of chromosome 22 in CML.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the 23 pairs of human chromosomes; the gene for p16 is located on its short arm (9p3).&lt;SEP&gt;A chromosome that breaks off and trades places with chromosome 22, contributing to the formation of the BCR::ABL1 gene.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-075</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682915</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chromosome 22">
      <data key="d0">Chromosome 22</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">A chromosome that breaks off and trades places with a piece of chromosome 9 in CML, resulting in the Philadelphia chromosome.&lt;SEP&gt;A chromosome that breaks off and switches places with a piece of chromosome 9, forming the Philadelphia chromosome.&lt;SEP&gt;A chromosome that breaks off and trades places with chromosome 9, resulting in the Philadelphia chromosome and BCR::ABL1 gene.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-075</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682915</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="BCR::ABL1">
      <data key="d0">BCR::ABL1</data>
      <data key="d1">gene</data>
      <data key="d2">A fused gene formed by translocation between chromosomes 9 and 22, producing a protein that leads to uncontrolled blood cell growth.&lt;SEP&gt;A fused gene created by translocation between chromosomes 9 and 22.&lt;SEP&gt;A fused gene created by the translocation of pieces of chromosomes 9 and 22, leading to the production of an abnormal protein that causes uncontrolled blood cell growth, characteristic of CML.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-074&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-075</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682915</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The most common type of lung cancer, a carcinoma arising from cells lining the airways.&lt;SEP&gt;A group of cancers that are the most common type of lung cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of lung cancer that includes subtypes such as adenocarcinoma, squamous cell carcinoma, and large cell carcinoma.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-019</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682915</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lung Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Lung Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancer that forms in tissues of the lung, usually in the cells lining air passages.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer that starts in the cells of the lungs; almost all are carcinomas.&lt;SEP&gt;A disease characterized by uncontrolled cell growth in lung tissues, with types including non-small cell lung cancer and small cell lung cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A general term for cancers that start in the lungs, including SCLC and NSCLC.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer of the lungs, linked to smoking and vaping.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cancer that occurs in the lungs, with increased risk from smoking or vaping.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cancer that occurs in the lungs. Smoking and vaping increase the chances of developing lung cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-129</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682915</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Small Cell Lung Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Small Cell Lung Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Another type of lung cancer, different from NSCLC.&lt;SEP&gt;A fast-dividing cancer of neuroendocrine cells; the second most common type of lung cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A fast-dividing lung cancer that arises from neuroendocrine cells, often associated with smoking.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-019</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682915</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bronchi">
      <data key="d0">Bronchi</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Airways in the lungs that branch from the trachea.&lt;SEP&gt;Two main airways that branch from the trachea into each lung.&lt;SEP&gt;Two large breathing tubes connecting the windpipe to the lungs.&lt;SEP&gt;Two airways that branch from the trachea into the lungs.&lt;SEP&gt;Breathing passages in the lungs, examined during bronchoscopy and panendoscopy.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-054</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682915</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bronchioli">
      <data key="d0">Bronchioli</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Smaller airways in the lungs that branch from bronchi.&lt;SEP&gt;Smaller airways that branch from the bronchi within the lungs.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-020</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682915</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Alveoli">
      <data key="d0">Alveoli</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Air sacs at the end of bronchioli where oxygen transfer occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;Small sacs at the end of bronchioli where oxygen is transferred to the blood.&lt;SEP&gt;Small air sacs at the end of bronchioles where oxygen is transferred into the blood.&lt;SEP&gt;Tiny air sacs in the lungs where gas exchange occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;Air sacs at the end of bronchioli where oxygen is transferred to blood.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-020</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682915</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Trachea">
      <data key="d0">Trachea</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Windpipe that carries air to the bronchi.&lt;SEP&gt;Windpipe that carries air from the throat to the bronchi.&lt;SEP&gt;The windpipe that splits into the bronchi.&lt;SEP&gt;Windpipe through which air travels to the bronchi.&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as the windpipe, it leads to the lungs.&lt;SEP&gt;The windpipe, part of the airway examined during bronchoscopy and panendoscopy.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-054</data>
