    <node id="Airways">
      <data key="d0">Airways</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Series of tubes in the respiratory system through which air travels, including bronchi and bronchioli.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-017</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682919</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lymphoblasts">
      <data key="d0">Lymphoblasts</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lymphoblasts are immature white blood cells that normally mature into lymphocytes. In the context of disease, they are most notably associated with acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL), where they are produced in excess and accumulate in the bone marrow, crowding out normal bone marrow cells and other blood cells. A diagnosis of ALL typically requires the presence of 20% or more lymphoblasts in the bone marrow. Additionally, lymphoblasts can be increased in the blast phase of chronic myeloid leukemia (CML), where they appear as a type of blast cell. These cells are considered abnormal when present in elevated numbers, reflecting their role as immature precursors in leukemic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-058&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-065&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-074&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-075&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-076&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-077</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682920</data>
