      <data key="d5">1788682946</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bloodstream">
      <data key="d0">Bloodstream</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The system of blood vessels through which cancer cells can spread to other parts of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Leukemia can spread outside the bloodstream.&lt;SEP&gt;The blood circulatory system that cancer cells use to travel to distant areas in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The circulatory system where calcium is released and transported.&lt;SEP&gt;The system of blood vessels through which nutrients and cancer cells can travel.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-157&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-162</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682946</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Genes">
      <data key="d0">Genes</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Instructions that tell new cells what to become and what to do, passed down from biological parents.&lt;SEP&gt;Instructions passed from biological parents to children that determine cell development and function.&lt;SEP&gt;Tiny parts of a cell that carry instructions for cell behavior and new cell production. Mutations in genes can lead to cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-160&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-174</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682946</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Family Health History">
      <data key="d0">Family Health History</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A record of health information about a person's family, which can change and should be updated with health care providers.&lt;SEP&gt;Information about a patient's family medical history, which should be asked for all rectal cancer patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Information about a patient's family medical history, relevant for rectal cancer risk assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;Information about diseases in a family, used to assess risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Information about health issues in blood relatives.&lt;SEP&gt;Information about health conditions in biological family members, used to assess cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-060&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-061&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-105&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-122</data>
