    <node id="Epithelium">
      <data key="d0">Epithelium</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Innermost lining of the mucosa, normally made of squamous cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Layer of cells lining the esophagus where cancer starts.&lt;SEP&gt;A thin, moist layer of cells that covers the inside of the gallbladder and bile ducts.&lt;SEP&gt;The surface layer of the oral mucosa containing stratified squamous cells.&lt;SEP&gt;The surface layer of tissue lining the inside of the mouth, where squamous cell carcinoma starts.&lt;SEP&gt;The surface layer of tissue surrounding the ovaries where most ovarian cancers are found.&lt;SEP&gt;The surface layer of tissue surrounding the ovaries where most ovarian cancers start.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-040</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682948</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lamina Propria">
      <data key="d0">Lamina Propria</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Thin layer of connective tissue under the epithelium.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of connective tissue found under the epithelium.&lt;SEP&gt;The bottom layer of connective tissue in the oral mucosa.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of connective tissue under the epithelium, containing stomach glands.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-162</data>
