    <node id="Thymus">
      <data key="d0">Thymus</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A small organ in the upper chest where lymphocytes develop into T lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;An organ in the lymphatic system.&lt;SEP&gt;A small organ in front of the windpipe that can become enlarged in T-ALL, potentially causing breathing problems.&lt;SEP&gt;A small organ in front of the windpipe, can be enlarged in T-ALL.&lt;SEP&gt;A small organ in front of the windpipe that can be enlarged in T-ALL.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-076</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682976</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tonsils">
      <data key="d0">Tonsils</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Small masses of lymph tissue at the back of the throat that help trap disease-causing germs.&lt;SEP&gt;Part of the lymphatic system.&lt;SEP&gt;Part of the oropharynx, located in the throat.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphoid tissues located in the throat, part of the oropharynx.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymphoid tissues in the throat that can be affected by HPV-related cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Part of the oropharynx.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-126</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682976</data>
