    <node id="Muscle (Muscularis)">
      <data key="d0">Muscle (Muscularis)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of soft tissue in the walls of the gallbladder and bile ducts.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-023</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682976</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Perimuscular Fibrous Tissue">
      <data key="d0">Perimuscular Fibrous Tissue</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of connective tissue that surrounds muscle in the gallbladder and bile ducts.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-023</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682976</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Serosa">
      <data key="d0">Serosa</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An outer membrane that covers the gallbladder and bile ducts, also called the serous membrane or visceral peritoneum.&lt;SEP&gt;A membrane also called the serous membrane or visceral peritoneum, which is a thin layer covering a surface.&lt;SEP&gt;The outer layer of the colon wall, also called adventitia.&lt;SEP&gt;The outer membrane covering the stomach, allowing smooth movement against other organs.&lt;SEP&gt;The outermost layer of the stomach wall.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-124&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-162&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-163</data>
