    <node id="FDG-PET/CT">
      <data key="d0">FDG-PET/CT</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">FDG-PET/CT is a combined positron emission tomography (PET) and computed tomography (CT) imaging modality that utilizes the radiotracer fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG), specifically the F-18 labeled form, to detect and assess metabolic activity in the body. This imaging test is primarily used in oncology to identify cancerous lesions, as malignant cells typically exhibit increased glucose uptake and metabolism, which the FDG tracer highlights. The integration of PET and CT allows for the precise localization of abnormal metabolic activity within the anatomical context provided by the CT scan.

This diagnostic tool is particularly valuable in the evaluation of suspected extramedullary leukemia, which refers to leukemic infiltration occurring outside the blood and bone marrow. In such clinical scenarios, FDG-PET/CT is employed when other imaging results are inconclusive or when there is a need to confirm the presence and extent of disease outside the primary hematopoietic sites. The scan is also broadly useful for detecting cancer activity in various other contexts, aiding in diagnosis, staging, and treatment planning.

A key procedural requirement for FDG-PET/CT is that the patient must fast for at least four hours prior to the scan. This fasting period is essential to ensure optimal tracer uptake by malignant tissues while minimizing interference from normal glucose metabolism, thereby enhancing the accuracy and clarity of the imaging results. Overall, FDG-PET/CT serves as a powerful and specific diagnostic tool, particularly when standard imaging methods are insufficient or when a high degree of metabolic detail is required.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-068&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-072&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-129&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-156</data>
