      <data key="d5">1788682994</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fertility Preservation">
      <data key="d0">Fertility Preservation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Fertility preservation refers to the range of actions, methods, and processes undertaken to safeguard a person’s ability to have biological children in the future, most commonly discussed and implemented before cancer treatment that may impair fertility. This practice is centered on keeping reproductive options open for later in life, particularly for patients who are at risk of infertility due to medical interventions such as chemotherapy, radiation, or surgery. The core objective is to protect or save eggs, sperm, or reproductive tissue so that individuals can potentially conceive biological children after their treatment concludes.

The specific techniques involved in fertility preservation include the collection and freezing of sperm or eggs, as well as more advanced procedures such as ovarian tissue banking and ovarian transposition. These methods are designed to enable future pregnancy by preserving reproductive cells or tissues prior to the start of cancer therapy. The process is typically discussed with patients before they begin treatment, ensuring that they are informed of their options and can make proactive decisions about their reproductive health. While the primary context is cancer care, the underlying principle of fertility preservation is broadly applicable to anyone seeking to maintain the possibility of having children later in life, whether due to medical reasons or personal choice.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-061&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-069&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-101&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-128&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-135&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-149&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-154&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-171&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-188</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
