    <node id="Cancer Treatment">
      <data key="d0">Cancer Treatment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Treatments such as radiation therapy and chemotherapy that can have side effects on fertility and other body functions.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical interventions such as chemotherapy, radiation, or surgery used to treat cancer, which may affect fertility.&lt;SEP&gt;Therapies for cancer that may cause bone damage, as mentioned in the context of bone scans.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical interventions such as chemotherapy that can affect fertility and require precautions during treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;General term for therapies used to treat cancer, including targeted therapies and immunotherapies.&lt;SEP&gt;Treatment based on tumor location, including various modalities such as surgery, radiation, and chemotherapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical interventions to treat cancer, which may be affected by smoking.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-084&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-101&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-105&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-127&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-178&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682996</data>
