    </node>
    <node id="Menstruation">
      <data key="d0">Menstruation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The monthly shedding of the uterine lining; may stop during cancer treatment but often returns within 2 years in those 35 and under.&lt;SEP&gt;The monthly shedding of the uterine lining, also known as a period, which may stop during cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;The monthly shedding of the uterine lining, which may stop during treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-101</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682996</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sperm">
      <data key="d0">Sperm</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Male reproductive cells that can be damaged by cancer treatment, affecting fertility.&lt;SEP&gt;Male reproductive cells that can be damaged by cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Reproductive cells from the testicles that are part of semen.&lt;SEP&gt;Male reproductive cells that are transported by semen.&lt;SEP&gt;Male reproductive cells; can be damaged by chemotherapy, causing infertility.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-089&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-101&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-155&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-188</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
