    <node id="Fertility Specialist">
      <data key="d0">Fertility Specialist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Fertility Specialist is a medical professional specializing in fertility and reproductive health, whose primary role is to help patients understand, discuss, and preserve their fertility, particularly in the context of medical treatments that may compromise reproductive capacity. This specialist is frequently consulted before cancer treatment, where they guide patients through fertility preservation options, and also assists individuals in exploring fertility options prior to starting endocrine therapy. As an expert in helping people conceive, the Fertility Specialist can explain various options for having a baby during or after treatment, addressing both the medical and practical aspects of family building. The specialist may be a doctor focused on fertility issues, and their expertise is often sought to ensure that patients are fully informed about their reproductive choices before undergoing procedures or therapies that could impact their ability to have children.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-101&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-111&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-128&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-154&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-157&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-171&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-196</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788682998</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ovaries">
      <data key="d0">Ovaries</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Ovaries are female reproductive organs located in the pelvis, typically grape-sized, that play a central role in sexual reproduction and endocrine function. They produce eggs (oocytes) necessary for fertilization and release key hormones, including estrogen and progesterone, which regulate the menstrual cycle and support secondary sexual characteristics. These organs are integral to the female reproductive system and are the primary site where ovarian cancer originates; their size, shape, and position are routinely assessed during a pelvic exam.

Ovaries are significantly impacted by cancer treatments. Radiation therapy can damage them, potentially leading to infertility, while chemotherapy and other treatments may also affect their function, impairing both fertility and hormone production. In surgical contexts, ovaries may be removed during procedures such as ovarian cancer surgery, pelvic exenteration, or radical cystectomy if cancer has spread. During a hysterectomy, ovaries may be either removed or left in place; their removal induces surgical menopause due to the sudden loss of hormone production. Additionally, women with Lynch syndrome have an elevated risk of developing cancer in the ovaries. Overall, the ovaries are vital for reproduction and hormonal balance, and their health is a key consideration in cancer treatment planning and surgical decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-060&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-101&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-112&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-122&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-135&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-140&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-144&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-155&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-181&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-185&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-188</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683002</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Testicles">
      <data key="d0">Testicles</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Testicles are the male reproductive organs responsible for producing sperm and hormones, including testosterone. They are a key component of the male reproductive system. These organs can be affected by cancer and its treatments, such as radiation therapy and chemotherapy, which may damage sperm production and fertility. Additionally, testicles are a site where Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL) can be found or affect the organs, indicating that they can be involved in certain cancers beyond primary testicular cancer. Overall, the testicles serve dual roles in reproduction and endocrine function, and they are vulnerable to damage from oncological treatments and disease infiltration.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-058&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-060&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-065&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-077&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-101</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683003</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Contrast Material">
      <data key="d0">Contrast Material</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Contrast Material refers to substances used to improve the clarity and quality of imaging pictures of the inside of the body, particularly in computed tomography (CT) and magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) scans. These agents are not dyes and are not permanent; they are administered either orally or through a vein to enhance the visibility of internal organs and structures. Different types of contrast material are formulated specifically for use in CT versus MRI scans. The substances are excreted from the body in urine. In certain clinical situations, such as when a patient has a serious allergy or poor kidney function, the use of contrast material may be avoided to prevent adverse reactions or complications.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-071&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-102&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-128&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-129&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-155</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683005</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Panoramic Dental X-ray">
      <data key="d0">Panoramic Dental X-ray</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An x-ray that captures the entire mouth in one image, used by dentists and oral surgeons.&lt;SEP&gt;An x-ray that captures the entire mouth in one image using a small dose of radiation, used by dentists and oral surgeons.&lt;SEP&gt;A dental x-ray that captures the entire mouth in one image using a small dose of radiation. It is used by dentists and oral surgeons for planning treatments like dentures, braces, extractions, and implants.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-129</data>
