    <node id="Open MRI">
      <data key="d0">Open MRI</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">An MRI machine with a magnetic top and bottom, allowing openings on each end.&lt;SEP&gt;An MRI machine with a magnetic top and bottom, allowing an opening on each end.&lt;SEP&gt;An MRI machine with magnets above and below, leaving open sides for patients with claustrophobia.&lt;SEP&gt;An MRI machine with a magnetic top and bottom, allowing openings on each end, used to reduce claustrophobia.&lt;SEP&gt;An MRI machine with a magnetic top and bottom, allowing for an opening and less enclosed space.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of MRI machine with a magnetic top and bottom, allowing an opening on each end, which may be more comfortable for patients with claustrophobia.&lt;SEP&gt;An MRI machine with a magnetic top and bottom, allowing openings on each end, designed to accommodate patients with claustrophobia.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-071&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-072&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-155&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-156</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683007</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Primary Tumor">
      <data key="d0">Primary Tumor</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Primary Tumor refers to the original mass of cancer cells formed at the site where cancer first began, distinguishing it from secondary growths or metastases. It is the initial tumor and the main area of cancer growth, serving as the primary reference point for staging the extent of the disease. This tumor is the original site of cancer growth from which cancer cells may spread to other parts of the body. In the context of staging, the primary tumor's extent is a key component in determining the overall cancer stage. While the term generally applies to any cancer's starting point, it can specifically describe tumors located in particular anatomical regions, such as a mass formed by cancer cells within the oropharynx or the initial tumor formed in the nasopharynx.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-090&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-094&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-095&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-096&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-104&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-126&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-158</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683008</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Radioactive Drug">
      <data key="d0">Radioactive Drug</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A substance used in PET scans to detect cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A tracer is a radioactive drug injected into a vein.&lt;SEP&gt;A substance injected into a vein for PET imaging to make cancer cells visible as bright spots.&lt;SEP&gt;A drug injected into a vein for PET scans to see where cancer cells are.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-115&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-177</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683008</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sugar">
      <data key="d0">Sugar</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Glucose used by cancer cells for growth, detected by PET scans.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer cells take up sugar, which is measured by PET scans.&lt;SEP&gt;A carbohydrate that the liver processes for energy.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-160</data>
