      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Claustrophobia">
      <data key="d0">Claustrophobia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Claustrophobia is a dread or fear of enclosed spaces, a condition that holds particular relevance in the context of medical imaging, specifically regarding Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI). This phobia can significantly affect a patient's ability to undergo an MRI, particularly when using a closed MRI scanner, which features a narrow, tube-like structure. Consequently, claustrophobia is a key factor that may influence a patient's choice between a closed MRI and an open MRI, as the latter provides a less confining environment.

The presence of claustrophobia is a critical consideration for both patients and their care teams when planning an MRI. Because closed MRI machines are more common than open ones, patients who experience this fear are advised to proactively discuss their condition with their healthcare providers before the procedure. This discussion allows the care team to make necessary accommodations or recommend alternative imaging options to ensure the patient's comfort and successful completion of the scan.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-072&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-102&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-129&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-155&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-156</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683011</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Distant Sites">
      <data key="d0">Distant Sites</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Areas of the body far from the primary tumor where cancer may spread.&lt;SEP&gt;Spread of cancer to distant sites, one of the main areas of cancer growth in staging.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-045</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683011</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bladder">
      <data key="d0">Bladder</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The bladder is a hollow, balloonlike organ located in the pelvis that stores urine until it is released from the body. In adults, it can hold up to 2 cups of urine. It is part of the urinary tract, situated near the prostate in males and near the cervix in females. The bladder normally appears bright on PET scans and is involved in the excretion of contrast material used in imaging studies. It may be affected by radiation therapy, particularly when treating nearby pelvic structures, and can be invaded by advanced anal tumors (stage IIIB). The bladder is also a key site for cancer, with bladder cancer originating in its lining. It is examined during cystoscopy and imaging for signs of malignancy, and it may be removed during radical cystectomy for bladder cancer or as part of pelvic exenteration.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-063&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-072&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-135&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-138&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-144&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-173&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-174&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-176&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-177&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-178&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-180&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-185&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-188</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683013</data>
