    <node id="Head and Neck Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Head and Neck Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancers of the head and neck region, linked to smoking and vaping.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancers occurring in the head and neck region, often affecting hearing and treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cancer that occurs in the head and neck region, which can affect jaw, teeth, and gums health.&lt;SEP&gt;A group of cancers that arise in the head or neck area, including cancers of the oral cavity, oropharynx, nasal cavity, nasopharynx, larynx, and hypopharynx.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancers that occur in the head and neck region, including nasopharyngeal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cancer caused by HPV.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cancer caused by HPV, affecting the head and neck region.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-126&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-130&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-133&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-185</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683013</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bone Scan">
      <data key="d0">Bone Scan</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Bone Scan is a nuclear medicine imaging test that uses a radioactive tracer, or radiotracer, to detect bone abnormalities, with a primary focus on identifying whether cancer has spread (metastasized) to the bones. The procedure is typically performed when a patient presents with symptoms such as bone pain or when they are considered to be at high risk for bone metastasis. During the scan, the radiotracer is injected, and areas of bone damage or abnormal activity appear as bright spots on the resulting images, helping clinicians pinpoint the location and extent of any cancerous involvement.

The test is also used more broadly to detect other bone abnormalities beyond cancer spread, serving as a general diagnostic tool for skeletal issues. However, its necessity is context-dependent: a Bone Scan may be deemed unnecessary if an FDG-PET/CT scan has already clearly demonstrated the presence of cancer in the bone, as the PET/CT result would already provide the required diagnostic information. In some clinical settings, the Bone Scan can be replaced by a sodium fluoride PET-CT, which offers an alternative imaging approach for similar indications. Ultimately, the decision to perform a Bone Scan is guided by clinical judgment, often triggered by specific symptoms or a high likelihood of metastatic disease, ensuring that the test is used efficiently within the broader diagnostic pathway.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-053&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-082&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-083&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-090&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-091&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-100&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-101&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-102&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-103&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-129&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-155&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-178</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
