    <node id="Gene">
      <data key="d0">Gene</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">A segment of DNA that contains coded instructions for making proteins.&lt;SEP&gt;Coded instructions for proteins, located on chromosomes.&lt;SEP&gt;A segment of DNA that can have mutations affecting how it works, as analyzed by next-generation sequencing.&lt;SEP&gt;Segments of DNA that code for proteins.&lt;SEP&gt;Segments of DNA that provide instructions for making proteins.&lt;SEP&gt;A segment of DNA that codes for proteins; genes can be mutated or overexpressed.&lt;SEP&gt;A unit of heredity; the text discusses genes such as BRCA and PIK3CA.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-054&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-070&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-092&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-104&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-105&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-130</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683015</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Side Effects">
      <data key="d0">Side Effects</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Side Effects are unwanted or adverse effects that can occur as a result of medical treatment, particularly in the context of cancer care. These effects are typically caused by therapies such as chemotherapy, PARP inhibitors, radiation, systemic therapy, and intravesical treatments like BCG. Common manifestations include nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, fatigue, weakness, hair loss, mouth sores, fever, chills, vision problems, infections, low blood cell counts, neuropathy, and urinary issues. The likelihood and severity of these side effects can be increased by patient behaviors such as smoking and vaping, and they are generally more pronounced in individuals who smoke. While the specific symptoms vary depending on the type of treatment and the patient’s health, side effects represent the unintended physical consequences that may arise during the course of managing a disease.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-072&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-108&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-119&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-120&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-139&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-178&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-182</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683017</data>
