    <node id="Mutation">
      <data key="d0">Mutation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A mutation is a change or error in the genetic code, specifically within the DNA sequence, that can alter the function of a gene. This alteration can take various forms, including deletion, insertion, inversion, amplification, translocation, and point mutation. Mutations may occur spontaneously or be inherited, though they often arise on their own rather than being passed down from parents. While some mutations are harmless, others can damage gene function, disrupt normal cell behavior, and contribute to the development of diseases, most notably cancer. In the context of oncology, mutations are frequently associated with cancer progression, as they can cause cells to grow out of control and become malignant. For example, mutations in specific genes such as BRCA and PIK3CA are discussed in relation to cancer risk and treatment. Additionally, mutations can be abnormalities that lead to particular cancer types, such as causing glial cells to grow uncontrollably and result in glioma. Beyond their role in disease onset, mutations can also influence how cancers respond to treatment, making them critical factors in both diagnosis and therapeutic decision-making. Overall, a mutation represents a fundamental alteration in genetic material that may have significant implications for cellular function and health, particularly in the development and management of cancer and other diseases.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-054&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-070&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-092&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-104&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-105&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-112&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-130&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-164&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-165&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-168</data>
