    <node id="Genetic Testing">
      <data key="d0">Genetic Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Genetic Testing is a medical diagnostic process that analyzes DNA to identify inherited (germline) mutations, typically performed on normal tissue samples such as blood, saliva, cheek swabs, or urine. This form of testing is distinct from tumor mutation testing, as it focuses on determining whether an individual carries hereditary genetic changes that increase their risk for developing cancer. It is commonly used to detect mutations in BRCA genes and other cancer-related genes, and is recommended for all individuals diagnosed with ovarian cancer to guide clinical management.

The scope of genetic testing extends beyond hereditary risk assessment. In oncology, it is also utilized to analyze genetic changes and biomarkers within cancer cells—such as leukemia cells—to inform treatment decisions and prognosis. Additionally, genetic testing serves as a method to identify specific mutations linked to prostate cancer and other malignancies, helping to tailor therapeutic approaches. The test can be performed on various sample types, including blood, saliva, urine, or tumor tissue, depending on the clinical question.

Genetic testing is also valuable for identifying mutations that cause inherited cancer syndromes, and results are often relevant for family members, as knowing whether a relative has undergone testing can influence interpretation of one’s own results. Overall, genetic testing plays a critical role in cancer risk assessment, early detection, and personalized treatment planning across multiple cancer types.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-058&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-070&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-097&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-122&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-157&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-164&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-178&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-085</data>
