    <node id="Anatomic Staging">
      <data key="d0">Anatomic Staging</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Staging based on extent of cancer as defined by tumor size (T), lymph node status (N), and distant metastasis (M).&lt;SEP&gt;Staging based on the extent of cancer as defined by TNM.&lt;SEP&gt;A staging method based on the extent of cancer as defined by tumor size (T), lymph node status (N), and distant metastasis (M).&lt;SEP&gt;Anatomic staging is based on the extent of cancer as defined by tumor size (T), lymph node status (N), and distant metastasis (M).</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-106&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prognostic Staging">
      <data key="d0">Prognostic Staging</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Staging that includes anatomic TNM and assumes standard-of-care treatment; divided into clinical and pathologic.&lt;SEP&gt;Staging that includes anatomic TNM plus tumor grade and assumes standard-of-care treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;A staging method that includes anatomic TNM plus tumor grade and biomarker status (HER2, ER, PR), and assumes standard-of-care treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Prognostic staging includes anatomic TNM and often Epstein-Barr virus (EBV) levels in the blood, assuming standard-of-care treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-106&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Clinical Staging">
      <data key="d0">Clinical Staging</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The rating given before any treatment, based on physical exam, biopsy, and imaging tests.&lt;SEP&gt;Clinical staging is the rating given before any treatment, based on physical exam, biopsy, and imaging tests.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pathologic Staging">
      <data key="d0">Pathologic Staging</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Staging determined by examining tissue removed during surgery.&lt;SEP&gt;Pathologic staging is determined by examining tissue removed during surgery, providing more specific details about cancer size and lymph node status.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dental Checkups">
      <data key="d0">Dental Checkups</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Regular dental examinations recommended for patients with head and neck cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-031</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="TNM Staging">
      <data key="d0">TNM Staging</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A system for staging cancer based on tumor, node, and metastasis scores, used to determine numbered stages from 0 to 4.&lt;SEP&gt;A system used to stage squamous cell carcinoma of the nasopharynx, describing tumor extent (T), lymph node involvement (N), and metastasis (M).</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-132</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Resectable Tumor">
      <data key="d0">Resectable Tumor</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A tumor that can be removed completely with surgery.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Unresectable Tumor">
      <data key="d0">Unresectable Tumor</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A tumor that cannot be removed completely with surgery due to involvement of major vessels or critical structures.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Depth of Invasion">
      <data key="d0">Depth of Invasion</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A measure of how deep a tumor has grown into tissue layers, used in staging mouth cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T1">
      <data key="d0">T1</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tumor stage: 2 cm or less with DOI of 5 mm or less.&lt;SEP&gt;A T category indicating a tumor 2 cm or less in size.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-107</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T2">
      <data key="d0">T2</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tumor stage: 2 cm or less with DOI &gt;5 mm, or 2-4 cm with DOI ≤5 mm.&lt;SEP&gt;A T category indicating a tumor more than 2 cm but not more than 5 cm.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-107</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T3">
      <data key="d0">T3</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tumor stage: 2-4 cm with DOI &gt;5 mm, or &gt;4 cm with DOI ≤5 mm.&lt;SEP&gt;A T category indicating a tumor more than 5 cm in size.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-107</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T4a">
      <data key="d0">T4a</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Moderately advanced local disease: tumor &gt;4 cm with DOI &gt;5 mm or invades nearby structures like cortical bone, maxillary sinus, or facial skin.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T4b">
      <data key="d0">T4b</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Very advanced local disease: tumor invades masticator space, pterygoid plates, skull base, or encases internal carotid artery.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Regional Lymph Node">
      <data key="d0">Regional Lymph Node</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lymph nodes near the tumor; cancer spread to these nodes is lymph node metastasis.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Extranodal Extension">
      <data key="d0">Extranodal Extension</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Spread of cancer through the lymph node capsule into surrounding tissues.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Acute Myeloid Leukemia">
      <data key="d0">Acute Myeloid Leukemia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of blood cancer starting in stem cells of bone marrow, characterized by buildup of immature white blood cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cancer where abnormal changes stop immature white blood cells (myeloid blasts) from maturing, leading to a buildup of blasts in bone marrow and blood.&lt;SEP&gt;A fast-growing cancer with too many immature white blood cells in bone marrow and blood, a rare side effect of treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of blood cancer that starts in the stem cells of bone marrow.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of blood cancer that starts in the stem cells of bone marrow, characterized by abnormal changes that stop immature white blood cells from maturing, leading to a buildup of blasts and a shortage of healthy blood cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cancer that affects the blood and bone marrow, characterized by the rapid growth of abnormal white blood cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-067&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-072&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-073</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Myeloid Blasts">
      <data key="d0">Myeloid Blasts</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Immature white blood cells that accumulate in AML due to abnormal changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Immature white blood cells that are affected in AML, also called myeloblasts or blasts, which accumulate in the bone marrow and blood.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-067</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prognosis">
      <data key="d0">Prognosis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Prognosis is the likely course and outcome of a disease, such as cancer, serving as a prediction or forecast of how the condition will progress and resolve. It is a central concept in guiding treatment decisions, as it provides an expectation of the disease's trajectory and eventual result. The determination of a prognosis is informed by multiple clinical factors, including cancer staging, which helps predict the likely path of the disease. Additionally, biomarker and genetic tests are used to refine the prognosis, offering a more precise understanding of the disease's probable behavior based on the tumor's molecular characteristics. In essence, prognosis synthesizes information from staging and laboratory tests to articulate the anticipated course and outcome of the illness.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-072&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-085&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-090&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-106&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-108&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-157&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-164&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-169&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-171</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Acute Promyelocytic Leukemia">
      <data key="d0">Acute Promyelocytic Leukemia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A subtype of AML characterized by a specific genetic abnormality.&lt;SEP&gt;A rare subtype of AML characterized by the abnormal fusion gene PML::RARA.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-067</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Blastic Plasmacytoid Dendritic Cell Neoplasm">
      <data key="d0">Blastic Plasmacytoid Dendritic Cell Neoplasm</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A subtype of AML mentioned in the book.&lt;SEP&gt;An aggressive subtype of AML that can be found in blood, bone marrow, lymph nodes, and/or skin.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-067</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Internal Carotid Artery">
      <data key="d0">Internal Carotid Artery</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Major artery in the neck that can be encased by advanced tumors.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Skull Base">
      <data key="d0">Skull Base</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Anatomical region at the base of the skull that can be invaded by advanced tumors.&lt;SEP&gt;The base of the skull; tumor invasion into the skull base is a criterion for T4b stage.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Masticator Space">
      <data key="d0">Masticator Space</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Anatomical space in the head that can be invaded by advanced tumors.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pterygoid Plates">
      <data key="d0">Pterygoid Plates</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Bony projections in the skull that can be invaded by advanced tumors.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cortical Bone">
      <data key="d0">Cortical Bone</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Dense outer layer of bone that can be invaded by tumors.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mandible">
      <data key="d0">Mandible</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Lower jawbone that can be invaded by tumors.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Maxilla">
      <data key="d0">Maxilla</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Upper jawbone that can be invaded by tumors.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Maxillary Sinus">
      <data key="d0">Maxillary Sinus</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Air-filled space in the maxilla that can be involved by tumors.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Skin of Face">
      <data key="d0">Skin of Face</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Facial skin that can be involved in T4a stage.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lymph Node Metastasis">
      <data key="d0">Lymph Node Metastasis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancer that has spread to regional lymph nodes; distinct from distant metastasis.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer spread to lymph nodes.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Distant Metastasis">
      <data key="d0">Distant Metastasis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancer that has spread to distant parts of the body outside the neck.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer spread to distant organs.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer that has spread to body parts far from the primary tumor.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer that has spread to distant parts of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;A cancer spread to an area far from the primary tumor.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-094&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-096&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-158&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-160</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Head and Neck Cancers">
      <data key="d0">Head and Neck Cancers</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancers that arise in the head and neck region, which can spread to neck lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;A group of cancers that arise in the head or neck area of the body, named and treated based on tumor location.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-049</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stem Cells">
      <data key="d0">Stem Cells</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Immature cells in bone marrow that can develop into various blood cells; AML starts in these cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Undifferentiated cells that can develop into various cell types, including blood cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gene Mutations">
      <data key="d0">Gene Mutations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
