    <node id="Blood">
      <data key="d0">Blood</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Blood is a specialized bodily fluid and tissue that circulates throughout the body, playing essential roles in transporting oxygen and nutrients to cells while carrying away metabolic waste products. It is composed of plasma and formed elements, including red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets. Beyond transport, blood is integral to the immune system, defending against pathogens, and to hemostasis, preventing bleeding through clotting mechanisms. Blood also serves as a conduit for hormones, facilitating endocrine signaling, and can be a vehicle for the spread of cancer cells during metastasis, as seen in conditions like liver cancer.

In clinical and diagnostic contexts, blood is a versatile sample source. It is used for genetic testing, including mutation and predisposition testing, as well as tumor marker tests. For certain procedures, such as karyotyping, a blood sample (or bone marrow) is required because it provides living cells that can be cultured and grown. Blood is also a critical medium for monitoring hematologic malignancies; for instance, in acute myeloid leukemia (AML), it may contain an accumulation of immature blasts, while in acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL), the overproduction of lymphoblasts can crowd out normal blood cell production. Additionally, blood can harbor cancer cells or circulating tumor DNA, making it a key specimen for liquid biopsies. In therapeutic contexts, blood is a source for harvesting stem cells, which can be used in transplantation and regenerative treatments.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-064&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-065&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-067&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-072&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-074&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-075&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-076&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-092&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-104&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-105&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-120&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-138&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-160&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-178&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-059</data>
