      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A blood test that measures substances in the blood to provide information about kidney and liver function.&lt;SEP&gt;A screening test measuring up to 14 chemicals in the blood.&lt;SEP&gt;A screening test for many diseases that includes tests for up to 14 chemicals in the blood.&lt;SEP&gt;A blood test that measures chemicals, proteins, and other substances to assess organ function.&lt;SEP&gt;A blood test that measures chemicals, proteins, and other substances to check for health problems in areas like the kidneys or liver.</data>
