    <node id="Remission">
      <data key="d0">Remission</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">State where AML cells disappear, allowing blood and saliva testing for predisposition.&lt;SEP&gt;PCR is important when testing for treatment response or remission.&lt;SEP&gt;The goal of AML treatment, meaning no signs of cancer after treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;A state where cancer is no longer detectable, after which maintenance therapy may follow.&lt;SEP&gt;The goal of AML treatment, meaning no signs of cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A state where there are no symptoms or signs of cancer; may last for months or years.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-072&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-113</data>
