    <node id="Leukemic Meningitis">
      <data key="d0">Leukemic Meningitis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Swelling of the outer layer of the brain from leukemia, which can be shown by an MRI scan.&lt;SEP&gt;Swelling of the outer layer of the brain from leukemia.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-071</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683038</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Spinal Cord">
      <data key="d0">Spinal Cord</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The lining of the spinal cord is a rare site for leukemia spread.&lt;SEP&gt;The bundle of nerves that transmits messages between the brain and the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Part of the central nervous system; primary CNS lymphoma can occur here and may relapse in this area.&lt;SEP&gt;Part of the central nervous system that can be affected by primary CNS lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Part of the central nervous system. Gliomas can start in the brain or sometimes the spinal cord.&lt;SEP&gt;Part of the central nervous system where glial cells support nerve function and gliomas can develop.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-112&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-113&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-115&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-164&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-165</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683038</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
