    <node id="Catheter">
      <data key="d0">Catheter</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A thin, long tube placed in a large vein, often in the upper arm, to deliver systemic therapy, fluids, and blood products.&lt;SEP&gt;A thin tube used to deliver intraperitoneal chemotherapy, connected to a port in the abdomen.&lt;SEP&gt;A thin, long tube placed in the upper arm to deliver systemic therapy, fluids, and blood products.&lt;SEP&gt;A tube inserted into a continent urinary diversion to drain urine.&lt;SEP&gt;A tube inserted through the urethra or stoma to help empty the bladder or pouch.&lt;SEP&gt;A flexible tube used to drain urine from the bladder or pouch, or to deliver medicine into the bladder.&lt;SEP&gt;A tube used to deliver medicine directly into the bladder during intravesical therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-073&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-144&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-181&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-182&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-185</data>
