    </node>
    <node id="Antimetabolites">
      <data key="d0">Antimetabolites</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of chemotherapy that prevents the building blocks of DNA from being used.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of chemotherapy drugs that prevent the building blocks of DNA from being used.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of chemotherapy drugs that includes capecitabine, fluorouracil, gemcitabine, and methotrexate.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-073&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-110</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683038</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Anthracyclines">
      <data key="d0">Anthracyclines</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of chemotherapy that damages and disrupts DNA making, causing cell death; may cause heart issues.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of chemotherapy drugs that damage and disrupt the making of DNA, causing cell death.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of chemotherapy drugs that includes doxorubicin, doxorubicin liposomal injection, and epirubicin.</data>
