    <node id="Methotrexate">
      <data key="d0">Methotrexate</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Methotrexate is a chemotherapy drug that functions as an antimetabolite, primarily used in the treatment of several cancers, including acute myeloid leukemia (AML), primary CNS lymphoma, and bladder cancer. In the context of AML, it is administered as part of systemic therapy and can also be injected directly into the spinal fluid to target disease in the central nervous system. For primary CNS lymphoma, Methotrexate is the main chemotherapeutic agent, often given in high doses to achieve efficacy; however, such high-dose treatment carries a risk of organ damage, particularly affecting the kidneys and liver. Its mechanism of action in this setting involves blocking the body’s utilization of folate, which is essential for cancer cell proliferation. Additionally, Methotrexate is a component of the ddMVAC regimen, a combination chemotherapy protocol used for bladder cancer. Across all applications, Methotrexate remains a cornerstone cytotoxic agent, though its use requires careful monitoring due to potential systemic toxicities, especially at elevated doses.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-073&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-109&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-110&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-118&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-120&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-121&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-183</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683042</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
