    <node id="Fallopian Tubes">
      <data key="d0">Fallopian Tubes</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Long, thin tubes that catch eggs from the ovaries and transport them to the uterus.&lt;SEP&gt;Tubes connecting the ovaries to the uterus; their condition may be assessed via ultrasound.&lt;SEP&gt;Tubes connecting ovaries to the uterus, often removed during ovarian cancer surgery.&lt;SEP&gt;Female reproductive organs removed during pelvic exenteration.&lt;SEP&gt;Tubes that carry eggs from ovaries to uterus; may be removed during radical cystectomy if cancer has spread.&lt;SEP&gt;Tubes that connect the ovaries to the uterus; moved during ovarian transposition.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-144&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-181&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-188</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683042</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ovarian Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Ovarian Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Ovarian cancer is a disease characterized by the abnormal growth of malignant cells in the ovaries, and it can also originate in the fallopian tubes. This condition encompasses various types and subtypes, including high-grade serous carcinoma and high-grade endometrioid carcinoma, and is often linked to genetic factors such as germline mutations, particularly BRCA mutations, as well as Lynch syndrome. The disease may also be associated with a family history that could increase the risk of other cancers, such as prostate cancer.

Diagnosis of ovarian cancer typically involves imaging techniques and biopsy to confirm the presence of cancer cells. A notable challenge is that the disease often presents without symptoms until it reaches advanced stages, making early detection difficult. When symptoms do appear, they are discussed alongside diagnostic and treatment approaches in medical literature.

The condition is staged using a system that ranges from stage 1 to stage 4, with further substages, and treatment recommendations are based on these staging protocols. Standard treatment options include surgery, chemotherapy, and maintenance therapy, all of which are described in clinical guidelines. Overall, ovarian cancer is a complex disease with multiple subtypes, genetic associations, and a structured approach to diagnosis, staging, and management.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-085&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-092&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-122</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683044</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Uterus">
      <data key="d0">Uterus</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">The uterus is a female reproductive organ located in the pelvis, where a fetus grows and develops during pregnancy. It is a key component of the female reproductive system, with its lower part forming the cervix. The uterus is the site of fetal development, and its lining may be biopsied to rule out uterine cancer. 

In medical procedures, the uterus is commonly removed during a hysterectomy, and it may also be excised during ovarian cancer surgery, pelvic exenteration, or radical cystectomy if cancer has spread to surrounding tissues. Its removal is a standard part of these surgical interventions, reflecting its role as a central organ in reproductive and pelvic health.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-132&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-135&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-137&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-140&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-144&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-181&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-185</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683046</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cervix">
      <data key="d0">Cervix</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The cervix is the lower part of the uterus that connects to the vagina, forming a key component of the female reproductive system. It is a narrow structure that plays a critical role in reproductive health, as it opens during childbirth to allow passage of the baby. Anatomically, the cervix is composed of two main regions: the ectocervix (the outer part visible during examination) and the endocervix (the inner canal leading to the uterus). 

Clinically, the cervix is a central focus in gynecological care. It is routinely examined during pelvic exams and sampled via a Pap test to screen for abnormalities, particularly cervical cancer, which originates in this tissue. The cervix is also a primary site for human papillomavirus (HPV) infection, a major risk factor for cancer development. In addition to screening, the cervix is involved in diagnostic and surgical procedures: it is the site where dye is injected for sentinel node biopsy, and it is removed during a hysterectomy or a trachelectomy (a fertility-sparing surgery). Overall, the cervix serves as both a structural gateway and a key area for cancer prevention and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-132&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-133&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-134&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-135&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-137&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-138&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-140&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-142&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-187</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683049</data>
