      <data key="d0">Transvaginal Ultrasound</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An ultrasound where the probe is inserted into the vagina to get clearer images of the ovaries.&lt;SEP&gt;An imaging test that uses sound waves to make pictures of the inside of the body, with a probe inserted into the vagina to view the cervix and nearby areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-135</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683049</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Contrast Agent">
      <data key="d0">Contrast Agent</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A substance used in imaging tests to enhance picture clarity, administered orally or intravenously.&lt;SEP&gt;A substance injected into the bloodstream to make blood vessels, organs, and tissues stand out more clearly in MRI images.&lt;SEP&gt;A substance injected into the bloodstream to highlight areas in organs, blood vessels, or tissues during imaging tests, such as MRI.&lt;SEP&gt;A substance injected into the bloodstream before a CT scan to make areas of cancer easier to see.&lt;SEP&gt;A substance used in imaging scans to make pictures clearer.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical that highlights body tissues for the scanner, given through a needle into a vein.&lt;SEP&gt;A substance used in imaging tests to make pictures clearer, may cause allergic reactions.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-083&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-114&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-115&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-135&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-171&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-187</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683049</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ascites">
      <data key="d0">Ascites</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Abnormal fluid accumulation in the abdominal cavity, a possible sign of ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluid accumulation in the abdominal cavity, checked for cancer cells in staging.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-046</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683049</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Abdomen">
      <data key="d0">Abdomen</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Body area examined and imaged to detect ovarian cancer and its spread.&lt;SEP&gt;The body region whose lining can be involved in metastatic pancreatic cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The body region where para-aortic lymph nodes are located.&lt;SEP&gt;The body region containing the para-aortic lymph nodes, which may be affected by cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Body area scanned in CT or MRI to look for cancer spread.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-078&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-138&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-142&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-177</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683049</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vagina">
      <data key="d0">Vagina</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The vagina is a muscular canal in the female reproductive system, located in the pelvis, that leads from the cervix to the outside of the body. It serves as the passage for menstrual flow, receives the penis during intercourse, and acts as the birth canal through which babies are delivered. During a pelvic exam, the vagina is viewed with a speculum, and it is also the site where the urethra opens nearby, making it relevant for procedures such as cystoscopy insertion.

The vagina is clinically significant in several medical contexts. It can be a site for HPV infection and may be involved in the spread of cervical cancer. In advanced cases, the vagina may be partially removed during procedures such as hysterectomy, trachelectomy, or radical cystectomy if cancer has spread. It can also be invaded by advanced anal tumors, particularly in stage IIIB disease. In more extensive surgeries, such as pelvic exenteration, the vagina may be entirely removed and subsequently reconstructed.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-132&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-135&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-140&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-142&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-144&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-176&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-181&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-185&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-188</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sedative">
      <data key="d0">Sedative</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Medicine given to help patients relax during MRI if they feel nervous in enclosed spaces.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of medicine given to help patients relax, especially if they get nervous in enclosed spaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Medicine given to help patients relax during MRI if they are anxious in small spaces.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of medicine offered to patients who get nervous in tight spaces during imaging scans to help them relax.&lt;SEP&gt;A medication to help relax during procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Medicine given to help patients relax during MRI if they are nervous in small spaces.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-060&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-123&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-170&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-177</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ultrasound Probe">
      <data key="d0">Ultrasound Probe</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Hand-held device used in ultrasounds to emit sound waves and capture images.&lt;SEP&gt;A device inserted into the rectum to provide visual guidance during prostate biopsy.&lt;SEP&gt;A device inserted into the rectum to provide images during prostate biopsy and ultrasound imaging.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-084&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-091</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CT Scanner">
      <data key="d0">CT Scanner</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Large machine with a tunnel that rotates an x-ray beam to take cross-sectional images.&lt;SEP&gt;A large machine with a tunnel used for CT scans.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-177</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="MRI Scanner">
      <data key="d0">MRI Scanner</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Enclosed machine that uses magnets and radio waves to create detailed images.&lt;SEP&gt;A large machine with a tunnel in the middle used to perform MRI scans.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-083</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Intravenous Contrast">
      <data key="d0">Intravenous Contrast</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Contrast agent injected into a vein to enhance images during CT or MRI.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hives">
      <data key="d0">Hives</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A possible allergic reaction to contrast agents, causing itchy welts on the skin.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Allergic Reaction">
      <data key="d0">Allergic Reaction</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An adverse immune response to contrast agents, which can be rare but serious.&lt;SEP&gt;An adverse immune response to a substance, such as contrast material, which patients should report to their care team.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-155</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cancer Spread">
      <data key="d0">Cancer Spread</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The process by which cancer cells move beyond the original tumor site to other parts of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The extent to which cancer has spread beyond the cervix, influencing treatment decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-142</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Symptoms">
      <data key="d0">Symptoms</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Physical signs such as bloating, pelvic pain, and urinary urgency that may indicate ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical or mental features that indicate a disease or condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Indicators like frequent urination or sexual problems that may relate to prostate issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Signs of disease such as frequent urination, difficulty peeing or pooping, or sexual problems.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical or mental signs of illness that patients should report to their care team.&lt;SEP&gt;Problems or feelings that may be signs of disease, such as headaches, seizures, and muscle weakness, which can lead to glioma diagnosis.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-082&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-090&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-096&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-164</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Positron Emission Tomography">
      <data key="d0">Positron Emission Tomography</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A scan that shows how cells use sugar, often combined with CT or MRI for cancer staging.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Computed Tomography">
      <data key="d0">Computed Tomography</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An imaging technique using x-rays to produce detailed cross-sectional images.&lt;SEP&gt;The main imaging test used to see colon cancer in the body, using X-rays to take many pictures that a computer combines into one detailed image.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-123</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Magnetic Resonance Imaging">
      <data key="d0">Magnetic Resonance Imaging</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An imaging technique using magnetic fields and radio waves to produce detailed images.&lt;SEP&gt;An imaging test not often used for colon cancer treatment planning, but may be ordered to better look at the liver or rectum or if CT results are unclear.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-123</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chest X-Ray">
      <data key="d0">Chest X-Ray</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A fast and painless imaging test using small amounts of radiation to check if cancer has spread to the lungs.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Diagnostic Laparoscopy">
      <data key="d0">Diagnostic Laparoscopy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A minimally invasive procedure involving a tiny cut in the abdomen and a laparoscope to view the abdomen and take tissue samples for testing.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fine-Needle Aspiration (FNA) Biopsy">
      <data key="d0">Fine-Needle Aspiration (FNA) Biopsy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A biopsy using a very thin needle to remove a small tissue sample from a tumor.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Core Biopsy">
      <data key="d0">Core Biopsy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A biopsy using a hollow needle to remove tissue samples.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Paracentesis">
      <data key="d0">Paracentesis</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A procedure using a long, thin needle inserted through the skin of the belly to remove a fluid sample.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hereditary Ovarian Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Hereditary Ovarian Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Ovarian cancer caused by inherited gene mutations, most commonly in BRCA1 or BRCA2 genes, or Lynch syndrome.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="BRCA1">
      <data key="d0">BRCA1</data>
      <data key="d1">gene</data>
      <data key="d2">A gene that, when mutated, increases the risk of developing ovarian, breast, and other cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene mutation that is a biomarker for guiding treatment in recurrent ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene that, when mutated, increases the risk of certain cancers, including prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene associated with hereditary breast and ovarian cancer; mutations also increase prostate cancer risk.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene associated with hereditary cancer risk.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene whose mutations increase risk of breast, ovarian, and other cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene mutation that, when present, makes PARP inhibitors a consideration for breast cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-084&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-085&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-092&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-105&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-111</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="BRCA2">
      <data key="d0">BRCA2</data>
      <data key="d1">gene</data>
      <data key="d2">A gene that, when mutated, increases the risk of developing ovarian, breast, and other cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene mutation that is a biomarker for guiding treatment in recurrent ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene that, when mutated, increases the risk of certain cancers, including prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene associated with hereditary breast and ovarian cancer; mutations also increase prostate cancer risk.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene associated with hereditary cancer risk.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene whose mutations increase risk of breast, ovarian, and other cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene mutation that, when present, makes PARP inhibitors a consideration for breast cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-084&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-085&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-092&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-105&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-111</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Radiotracer">
      <data key="d0">Radiotracer</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A sugar-based substance put into the body through a vein that emits a small amount of energy detected by imaging machines.&lt;SEP&gt;A substance that releases small amounts of radiation, used in bone scans.&lt;SEP&gt;A substance that releases small amounts of radiation, injected into a vein for bone scans.&lt;SEP&gt;A radioactive substance used in PET scans to visualize cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A radioactive substance used in PET scans, often a sugar that is injected into the body and taken up by cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-101&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-102&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-134&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-135&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-155</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Laparoscope">
      <data key="d0">Laparoscope</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A thin tube with a light and camera used in laparoscopy to view the abdomen.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Somatic Mutations">
      <data key="d0">Somatic Mutations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Mutations in the tumor itself, as opposed to germline mutations, tested in the tumor tissue.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Germline Mutations">
      <data key="d0">Germline Mutations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Inherited mutations present in all cells, tested through blood, saliva, or cheek swab.&lt;SEP&gt;Gene mutations inherited from biological parents.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-105</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Maintenance Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Maintenance Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Treatment given after initial treatment to keep cancer from returning; decisions may be guided by BRCA status.&lt;SEP&gt;Treatment given after initial treatment to keep cancer from returning; guided by biomarkers.&lt;SEP&gt;Additional treatment after initial therapy to keep cancer from returning, may be an option for advanced cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;Treatment given after remission to prevent cancer recurrence.&lt;SEP&gt;Ongoing treatment after initial chemotherapy to prevent recurrence.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic therapy after successful initial treatment to reduce risk of cancer recurrence or extend time until progression.&lt;SEP&gt;Ongoing intravesical BCG or chemotherapy treatments given periodically to prevent cancer recurrence.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-182</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nutritional Health">
      <data key="d0">Nutritional Health</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The state of a patient's diet and eating habits, which can be affected by ovarian cancer symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Positron Emission Tomography (PET)">
      <data key="d0">Positron Emission Tomography (PET)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An imaging technique that uses a radiotracer to show cellular activity, often combined with CT or MRI.&lt;SEP&gt;An imaging test that uses small amounts of radioactive materials called radiotracers to see how tissues and organs are functioning.&lt;SEP&gt;An imaging test that uses radioactive glucose to detect cancer cells, which appear brighter due to higher sugar uptake.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-135&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-187</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Breast Cancer Gene 1 (BRCA1)">
      <data key="d0">Breast Cancer Gene 1 (BRCA1)</data>
      <data key="d1">gene</data>
      <data key="d2">A gene that, when mutated, increases the risk of developing ovarian, breast, and other cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Breast Cancer Gene 2 (BRCA2)">
      <data key="d0">Breast Cancer Gene 2 (BRCA2)</data>
      <data key="d1">gene</data>
      <data key="d2">A gene that, when mutated, increases the risk of developing ovarian, breast, and other cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-042</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="BRCA Genes">
      <data key="d0">BRCA Genes</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Genes that, when mutated, increase the risk of hereditary cancers, particularly ovarian and breast cancer. Mutations in these genes are important biomarkers for ovarian cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Genes associated with hereditary ovarian cancer; mutations in these genes increase risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-044</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hereditary Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Hereditary Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancers caused by inherited genetic mutations, such as those in BRCA genes.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer resulting from inherited gene mutations, a small number of thyroid cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-146</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Registered Dietitian">
      <data key="d0">Registered Dietitian</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A healthcare professional who provides nutritional guidance and meal planning, referred to for patients needing help with diet.&lt;SEP&gt;A nutrition expert who provides dietary guidance for cancer patients.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gastrointestinal (GI) Tract">
      <data key="d0">Gastrointestinal (GI) Tract</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The system of organs through which food passes, including the stomach, small bowel, and large bowel.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-043</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683051</data>
      <data key="d6" />
