    <node id="Bevacizumab">
      <data key="d0">Bevacizumab</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A targeted therapy drug used in ovarian cancer treatment, often with chemotherapy.&lt;SEP&gt;A drug that inhibits blood vessel growth, used in combination with chemotherapy for ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A drug (also known as Avastin) that stops the growth of new blood vessels feeding tumors, used in chemotherapy and maintenance therapy for ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A targeted therapy (Avastin) used in treatment of recurrent ovarian cancer, often added to chemotherapy.&lt;SEP&gt;A targeted therapy drug (biologic) that works with chemotherapy, also known as Avastin.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-145</data>
