    <node id="Nasal Cavity">
      <data key="d0">Nasal Cavity</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The space behind the nose, where the pharynx starts.&lt;SEP&gt;The space inside the nose, lying above the hard palate and curving down at the back to join the throat.&lt;SEP&gt;The nasal cavity is a part of the respiratory system; nasopharyngeal cancer can spread to this area.&lt;SEP&gt;The inside of the nose, which the tumor may grow into in T1 stage of nasopharyngeal carcinoma.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-126&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-132</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683056</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Paranasal Sinuses">
      <data key="d0">Paranasal Sinuses</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Air-filled spaces around the nasal cavity, where head and neck cancer can occur.&lt;SEP&gt;Spaces around the nasal cavity where cancer can occur.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-126</data>
