    <node id="Human Papillomavirus (HPV)">
      <data key="d0">Human Papillomavirus (HPV)</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">A virus that is tested for in throat cancer patients, often through p16 testing.&lt;SEP&gt;A group of viruses that infect skin and mucous membranes, can cause warts and some cancers, including throat cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A virus that can cause throat cancer; p16-positive cancers are HPV-related.&lt;SEP&gt;A sexually transmitted infection that can cause cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A common sexually transmitted infection with over 100 strains, some high-risk types linked to cervical and other cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;A sexually transmitted virus that is extremely common and strongly linked with anal cancer. There are more than 100 strains, with high-risk forms including HPV16 and HPV18.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-132&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-133&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-185</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683056</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="p16">
      <data key="d0">p16</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A biomarker used in testing for HPV-related throat cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A protein marker used to classify throat cancers as p16-positive (HPV-related) or p16-negative (not HPV-related).</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056</data>
