      <data key="d0">Primary Care Physician (PCP)</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A physician who provides general care and is kept informed of the patient's cancer care.&lt;SEP&gt;A physician who provides general care and should be updated about changes in a patient's condition.&lt;SEP&gt;A physician who provides general medical care and coordinates with specialists.&lt;SEP&gt;A physician who provides general healthcare and coordinates patient care, including being informed of changes in the care team.&lt;SEP&gt;A doctor who provides general medical care and coordinates with specialists.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-075&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-096&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-098&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-100</data>
