    <node id="Oropharynx">
      <data key="d0">Oropharynx</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The oropharynx is a part of the throat located behind the mouth, forming the middle section of the pharynx. It includes the back of the roof of the mouth (soft palate), the tonsils, the side and back walls of the throat, and the base of the tongue. In some clinical contexts, it is simply referred to as "the throat." This anatomical region is not fully visible when the mouth is opened, so examination typically requires special tools, such as during a procedure called panendoscopy.

The oropharynx is clinically significant in several diseases. For instance, p16-negative throat cancer originates in this area. Additionally, in nasopharyngeal carcinoma, the tumor may grow into the oropharynx at the T1 stage, and nasopharyngeal cancer can spread to this region. As a key part of the upper aerodigestive tract, the oropharynx serves as a critical site for both diagnostic evaluation and understanding the progression of head and neck cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-048&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-049&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-050&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-054&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-126&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-128&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-132</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683058</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Anesthesiologist">
      <data key="d0">Anesthesiologist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A medical professional who administers anesthesia and conducts pre-anesthesia assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;A physician who administers anesthesia during surgery.&lt;SEP&gt;A doctor who gives anesthesia to prevent pain during surgery or procedures.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-108&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-176</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683058</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Depression">
      <data key="d0">Depression</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A mental health condition that may be experienced by cancer patients, characterized by persistent sadness and loss of interest.&lt;SEP&gt;A mood disorder that can be a symptom of primary CNS lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;A mental health condition characterized by persistent sadness and loss of interest.&lt;SEP&gt;A common psychological condition in people with cancer, characterized by persistent sadness and loss of interest.&lt;SEP&gt;A psychological condition that may affect cancer survivors.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-112&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-113&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-116&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-136&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-195&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-196</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683058</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Anxiety">
      <data key="d0">Anxiety</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A mental health condition that may be experienced by cancer patients, characterized by excessive worry and fear.&lt;SEP&gt;A mental health condition characterized by excessive worry and fear.&lt;SEP&gt;A common psychological condition in people with cancer, characterized by feelings of worry and unease.&lt;SEP&gt;A mental health condition characterized by excessive worry or fear.&lt;SEP&gt;A psychological condition that may affect cancer survivors.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-051&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-116&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-136&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-195&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-196</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683058</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sleep Issues">
      <data key="d0">Sleep Issues</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
