    <node id="Tumor Mutational Burden-High (TMB-H)">
      <data key="d0">Tumor Mutational Burden-High (TMB-H)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A classification for tumors with 10 or more mutations per million base pairs, often treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors.&lt;SEP&gt;A high number of mutations in a tumor, which may predict response to immunotherapy.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition where there are 10 or more mutations per million base pairs of tumor DNA.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-152&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-157</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Programmed Cell Death Protein 1 (PD-1)">
      <data key="d0">Programmed Cell Death Protein 1 (PD-1)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A protein on immune cells that, when bound to PD-L1, can inhibit immune response; targeted by some immune checkpoint inhibitors.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-055</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
