    <node id="Treatment">
      <data key="d0">Treatment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Medical care given to a patient for cancer, which can affect fertility.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical care given to a patient for an illness or condition.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical care aimed at stopping the activity of the BCR::ABL1 protein in CML and treating ALL.&lt;SEP&gt;Medical interventions such as surgery or radiation therapy for prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-055&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-075&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-085&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-072</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL)">
      <data key="d0">Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL)</data>
      <data key="d1">disease</data>
      <data key="d2">A fast-growing blood cancer that starts in lymphocytes, most common in children.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of blood cancer characterized by too many abnormal white blood cells called lymphoblasts.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-075&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-076</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="B-ALL">
      <data key="d0">B-ALL</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A subtype of ALL that starts in B cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of ALL that affects B-cell lymphocytes. It includes subtypes like BCR::ABL1-negative, BCR::ABL1-like, and BCR::ABL1-positive.&lt;SEP&gt;B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia, a type of ALL that starts in B-cell lymphocytes. More common than T-ALL.&lt;SEP&gt;B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia, a subtype of ALL that affects B-cell lymphoblasts.&lt;SEP&gt;B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia, a subtype of ALL that arises from B-cell lymphocytes.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-058&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-065&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-076&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-077</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T-ALL">
      <data key="d0">T-ALL</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A subtype of ALL that starts in T cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A group of cancers that start in T-cell lymphocytes. It is less common than B-ALL.&lt;SEP&gt;T-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia, a type of ALL that starts in T-cell lymphocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;T-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia, a subtype of ALL that starts in T-cell lymphocytes and can cause an enlarged thymus.&lt;SEP&gt;T-cell acute lymphoblastic leukemia, a subtype of ALL that arises from T-cell lymphocytes.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-058&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-065&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-076&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-077</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Carcinoma In Situ">
      <data key="d0">Carcinoma In Situ</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A stage of cancer where abnormal cells are present but have not spread to nearby tissue; denoted as Tis.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition where cancerous cells are found only in the squamous cell layer, indicated as Tis in TNM staging.&lt;SEP&gt;A flat patch of cancer cells on the surface of the bladder lining that is fast-growing and aggressive, also known as Stage 0is.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-132&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-179</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Resectable">
      <data key="d0">Resectable</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A term describing a tumor that can be completely removed with surgery.&lt;SEP&gt;Resectable means the tumor can be removed completely with surgery.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Unresectable">
      <data key="d0">Unresectable</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A term describing a tumor that cannot be completely removed with surgery due to involvement of nearby structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Unresectable means the tumor cannot be removed completely with surgery due to involvement of nearby structures.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Locoregional">
      <data key="d0">Locoregional</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A term referring to a tumor that has spread to tissue, organs, or lymph nodes in the head and neck.&lt;SEP&gt;Locoregional or locally advanced refers to a tumor that has spread to tissue, organs, or lymph nodes in the head and neck.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Metastatic">
      <data key="d0">Metastatic</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A term describing cancer that has spread to other parts of the body, such as the lung or distant lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Metastatic refers to cancer that has spread to other parts of the body, such as the lungs or distant lymph nodes.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Epiglottis">
      <data key="d0">Epiglottis</data>
      <data key="d1">bodypart</data>
      <data key="d2">A flap that closes the airway to the trachea; tumor growth into the epiglottis is a criterion for T3 stage.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Carotid Artery">
      <data key="d0">Carotid Artery</data>
      <data key="d1">bodypart</data>
      <data key="d2">A major artery in the neck; tumor encasement of the carotid artery is a criterion for T4b stage.&lt;SEP&gt;The carotid artery is a major blood vessel in the neck; cancer may involve it in advanced disease.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-056&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia">
      <data key="d0">Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A fast-growing blood cancer that starts in lymphocytes, characterized by overproduction of immature lymphocytes called lymphoblasts in the bone marrow.&lt;SEP&gt;A cancer of the blood and bone marrow that affects lymphoid progenitor cells, which develop into lymphocytes. It is characterized by the presence of lymphoblasts in the bone marrow, blood, and organs.&lt;SEP&gt;A fast-growing blood cancer that starts in lymphocytes, a type of white blood cell. In ALL, bone marrow makes too many immature lymphocytes called lymphoblasts, which can crowd out other blood cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A fast-growing blood cancer in which bone marrow makes too many immature lymphocytes called lymphoblasts.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-058&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-065&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="B-Cell ALL">
      <data key="d0">B-Cell ALL</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A subtype of ALL that starts in B-cell lymphocytes, more common than T-ALL.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T-Cell ALL">
      <data key="d0">T-Cell ALL</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A subtype of ALL that starts in T-cell lymphocytes, can cause enlarged thymus and breathing problems.&lt;SEP&gt;A subtype of ALL that starts in T-cell lymphocytes, can cause enlarged thymus.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Burkitt Leukemia">
      <data key="d0">Burkitt Leukemia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A rare subtype of mature B-cell ALL, essentially the same as Burkitt lymphoma but treated differently.&lt;SEP&gt;A rare subtype of mature B-cell ALL.&lt;SEP&gt;A rare subtype of mature B-cell ALL, essentially the same as Burkitt lymphoma but treated differently from B-ALL.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-065&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-075&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-076</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="B-Cell Lymphoblastic Lymphoma">
      <data key="d0">B-Cell Lymphoblastic Lymphoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A condition where B-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in lymph nodes instead of bone marrow, also called B-LL or B-LBL.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition where B-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in lymph nodes instead of bone marrow.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-076</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683063</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T-Cell Lymphoblastic Lymphoma">
      <data key="d0">T-Cell Lymphoblastic Lymphoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A condition where T-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in the thymus instead of bone marrow, also called T-LL or T-LBL.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition where T-cell lymphoblasts grow mostly in the thymus instead of bone marrow.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-057&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-076</data>
