      <data key="d2">A disease characterized by abnormal cell growth in the pancreas, with stages ranging from 0 to 4.&lt;SEP&gt;A disease characterized by uncontrolled growth of cells in the pancreas, often detected through a series of tests and managed by a multidisciplinary team.&lt;SEP&gt;A cancer that forms in the pancreas; mentioned as related to certain germline mutations.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cancer associated with BRCA mutations.</data>
