      <data key="d2">A specialist in the health care of older adults.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683073</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Palliative Care Provider">
      <data key="d0">Palliative Care Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A specialist focused on relieving symptoms and improving quality of life.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683073</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mental Health Provider">
      <data key="d0">Mental Health Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A professional who supports emotional and psychological well-being.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683073</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prostate Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Prostate Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Prostate Cancer is a disease in which cells in the prostate gland grow out of control, and it is one of the most common types of cancer. The condition can be early-stage (localized) or advanced-stage (metastatic), with the latter occurring when cancer spreads outside the prostate to other parts of the body, such as lymph nodes and bones, through a process called metastasis. Prostate cancer is often slow-growing and asymptomatic in its early stages, contributing to high survival rates when detected early. Risk factors for developing the disease include age, family history, genetic factors, race, and lifestyle. Detection and risk assessment involve various tests, including PSA (prostate-specific antigen) levels, biopsy, and grading, and the disease often requires staging and treatment. The condition is also a focus of risk assessment and genetic testing discussions, as it is characterized by the presence of prostate cancer cells and abnormal cell growth within the gland.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-081&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-082&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-083&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-084&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-085&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-086&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-089&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-090&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-091&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-092&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-093&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-094</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia (BPH)">
      <data key="d0">Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia (BPH)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A non-cancerous enlargement of the prostate that can cause urinary symptoms similar to prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition where the prostate is enlarged, causing urinary symptoms similar to prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Male Reproductive System">
      <data key="d0">Male Reproductive System</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The system of organs involved in reproduction, including the prostate, penis, seminal vesicles, and testicles.&lt;SEP&gt;Includes the prostate, penis, seminal vesicles, and testicles.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Enlarged Prostate">
      <data key="d0">Enlarged Prostate</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A condition where the prostate grows larger, also known as benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH), which can cause urinary symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition where the prostate is larger than normal, leading to higher PSA production.&lt;SEP&gt;Another term for benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH), which can cause urinary symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition where the prostate is enlarged, which can cause high PSA levels.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-086&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-089</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Semen">
      <data key="d0">Semen</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Fluid produced by the prostate and other glands that carries sperm.&lt;SEP&gt;A fluid made up of liquids from the prostate and seminal vesicles as well as sperm from the testicles. Released from the body through the urethra during ejaculation.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluid made up of liquids from the prostate and seminal vesicles as well as sperm from the testicles.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluid that transports sperm; PSA helps in this process.&lt;SEP&gt;Body fluid that may contain blood after biopsy.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluid containing sperm; collected and frozen in sperm banking.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-089&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-092&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-188</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Seminal Vesicles">
      <data key="d0">Seminal Vesicles</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Glands that produce fluid for semen.&lt;SEP&gt;Two glands that make another part of the fluid that becomes semen. Located above the prostate and behind the bladder.&lt;SEP&gt;Two glands that make and store fluid that becomes semen, located above the prostate and behind the bladder.&lt;SEP&gt;Two glands that make and store another part of the fluid that becomes semen, located above the prostate and behind the bladder.&lt;SEP&gt;Glands that help make semen; may be removed during radical cystectomy if cancer has spread.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-181</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Care Plan">
      <data key="d0">Care Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A personalized plan developed by the care team and patient to guide treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prostate Cancer Symptoms">
      <data key="d0">Prostate Cancer Symptoms</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Symptoms that may indicate prostate cancer, including blood in urine or semen, burning or pain while urinating, unexplained weight loss, and bone, hip, or back pain.&lt;SEP&gt;Symptoms may include blood in urine or semen, burning or pain while urinating, unexplained weight loss, bone, hip, or back pain.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Erectile Dysfunction">
      <data key="d0">Erectile Dysfunction</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Difficulty getting an erection, a possible symptom of prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Painful Ejaculation">
      <data key="d0">Painful Ejaculation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Pain during ejaculation, a possible symptom of prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prostate-Specific Antigen (PSA)">
      <data key="d0">Prostate-Specific Antigen (PSA)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A protein made by the prostate that nourishes and helps transmit semen.&lt;SEP&gt;A protein produced by the prostate gland; high levels in the blood may indicate prostate issues.&lt;SEP&gt;A protein made by the prostate gland; high levels in blood may indicate prostate cancer but not definitive.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-081&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-082</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Genetic Factors">
      <data key="d0">Genetic Factors</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Genetic changes (mutations) linked with prostate cancer. Inherited changes in the BRCA2 gene increase risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Race">
      <data key="d0">Race</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A risk factor for prostate cancer. In the US, Black males are more likely to develop and die from prostate cancer compared to white males.&lt;SEP&gt;A factor that influences PSA level, with normal levels differing between Black and white males.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-086</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Diet and Lifestyle">
      <data key="d0">Diet and Lifestyle</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Factors such as diet, exercise, smoking, and obesity that influence prostate cancer risk and aggressiveness.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Early-Stage Prostate Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Early-Stage Prostate Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Prostate cancer that has not spread beyond the prostate. Also called localized prostate cancer. It is highly treatable and often curable.&lt;SEP&gt;Prostate cancer that has not spread beyond the prostate, also called localized prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Advanced-Stage Prostate Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Advanced-Stage Prostate Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Prostate cancer that has spread outside the prostate to other areas. Includes regional and metastatic prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Prostate cancer that has spread beyond the prostate to other areas in the body, also called metastatic prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Prostate cancer that has spread outside the prostate to other areas. It is usually a life-long disease, but treatment can slow it down and reduce symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-089</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Localized Prostate Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Localized Prostate Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancer contained entirely within the prostate. Synonymous with early-stage prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Early-stage prostate cancer that stays within the prostate gland.&lt;SEP&gt;Prostate cancer that is confined to the prostate gland.&lt;SEP&gt;Prostate cancer that is contained entirely within the prostate and has not spread beyond it.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-081&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-085&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Metastatic Prostate Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Metastatic Prostate Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Prostate cancer that has spread to lymph nodes, bones, liver, lungs, and other organs.&lt;SEP&gt;Advanced-stage prostate cancer that has spread to other parts of the body, such as lymph nodes, bones, or organs.&lt;SEP&gt;Prostate cancer that has spread to other parts of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Prostate cancer that has spread beyond the prostate to other parts of the body, such as lymph nodes, bones, liver, or lungs.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-081&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-085&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Regional Prostate Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Regional Prostate Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancer that grows from the prostate to nearby lymph nodes but no farther. Also called locally advanced prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Prostate cancer that has spread to nearby lymph nodes or tissues.&lt;SEP&gt;Prostate cancer that has grown from the prostate to nearby areas such as lymph nodes but no farther.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-085&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="BRCA2 Gene">
      <data key="d0">BRCA2 Gene</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">A gene in which inherited genetic changes increase the risk of prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene in which inherited genetic changes increase the risk of developing prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Black Males">
      <data key="d0">Black Males</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A demographic group in the US more likely to develop prostate cancer, often at an earlier age and with more aggressive disease.&lt;SEP&gt;A demographic group noted to have higher normal PSA levels compared to white males.&lt;SEP&gt;Males of African descent in the United States who have a higher risk of developing and dying from prostate cancer compared to white males.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-086&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="White Males">
      <data key="d0">White Males</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A demographic group in the US with a lower risk of prostate cancer compared to Black males.&lt;SEP&gt;A demographic group with lower normal PSA levels compared to Black males.&lt;SEP&gt;Males of European descent in the United States who have a lower risk of prostate cancer compared to Black males.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-086&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hispanic Males">
      <data key="d0">Hispanic Males</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A demographic group in the US with a lower incidence of prostate cancer compared to white and Black males.&lt;SEP&gt;Males of Hispanic ethnicity in the United States who have a lower risk of prostate cancer compared to white and Black males.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Asian Males">
      <data key="d0">Asian Males</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A demographic group in the US with a lower incidence of prostate cancer compared to white and Black males.&lt;SEP&gt;Males of Asian descent in the United States who have a lower risk of prostate cancer compared to white and Black males.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prostate Gland">
      <data key="d0">Prostate Gland</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">A male reproductive organ that produces seminal fluid and PSA.&lt;SEP&gt;A gland in the male reproductive system that produces PSA; subject of cancer screening.&lt;SEP&gt;Another term for the prostate, the target of biopsy and cancer evaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;A gland in the male reproductive system that produces prostate-specific antigen and is the site where prostate cancer develops.&lt;SEP&gt;A male reproductive organ that can be affected by cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A gland in the male reproductive system located in the pelvis.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-081&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-082&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-084&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-089&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-093&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-185</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Active Surveillance">
      <data key="d0">Active Surveillance</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A management strategy for early-stage prostate cancer involving regular tests and no immediate treatment unless the cancer progresses.&lt;SEP&gt;A management strategy for low-risk prostate cancer involving regular monitoring without immediate treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;A management strategy for prostate cancer involving regular monitoring and repeat biopsies to track changes.&lt;SEP&gt;A management strategy for very-low-risk cancers involving close monitoring instead of immediate surgery.&lt;SEP&gt;A monitoring approach for small, low-risk cancers without immediate surgery.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-081&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-083&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-084&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-147&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-150</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hormone Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Hormone Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A treatment that reduces or blocks hormones to slow cancer growth.&lt;SEP&gt;A treatment for advanced-stage prostate cancer that aims to slow down its growth.&lt;SEP&gt;A systemic treatment that adds, blocks, or removes hormones to treat cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Treatment that blocks or lowers hormones to treat cancer, particularly prostate and breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-081&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-093&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-094</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
