    </node>
    <node id="PSA Test">
      <data key="d0">PSA Test</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A blood test measuring PSA levels to screen for prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A blood test measuring PSA levels to screen for prostate issues.&lt;SEP&gt;A blood test that measures prostate-specific antigen levels, used as a screening tool for prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A blood test that measures the amount of prostate-specific antigen (PSA) in the bloodstream. High levels may indicate prostate cancer, but it cannot diagnose alone.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-081&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-082&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-083&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-089</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683075</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prostate">
      <data key="d0">Prostate</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">The prostate is a gland in the male reproductive system, located just below the bladder in the pelvis, where it surrounds the urethra. Typically about the size of a ping-pong ball, this organ plays a crucial role in sexual reproduction by producing fluid that nourishes and transmits sperm, as well as contributing to the formation of semen. It also produces prostate-specific antigen (PSA) and contains muscles that help propel semen through the urethra during ejaculation.

The prostate is clinically significant as the site where prostate cancer originates and can be affected by other conditions, including benign enlargement. It is a primary target for cancer screening, often through PSA testing, and is subject to biopsy procedures for diagnostic purposes. In cases where cancer has spread, the prostate may be removed during a radical cystectomy. Overall, the prostate is essential for male fertility and is a key focus in urological health and cancer management.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-079&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-080&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-082&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-083&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-084&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-086&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-087&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-088&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-090&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-091&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-181</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
