    <node id="Digital Rectal Exam">
      <data key="d0">Digital Rectal Exam</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Digital Rectal Exam (DRE) is a clinical procedure in which a doctor inserts a gloved, lubricated finger into the patient's anus and rectum to physically assess the prostate gland and surrounding tissues. The primary purpose of this examination is to detect abnormalities in the prostate, such as irregularities, hardening, or changes in size and texture, which may indicate the presence of cancer or other pathological conditions. During the exam, the doctor feels the prostate through the rectal wall to evaluate its condition, making it a simple yet effective screening tool for prostate health.

Beyond its role in initial prostate screening, the Digital Rectal Exam is also utilized in the context of anal cancer. It serves as a clinical examination of the rectum and anus to detect or assess growths or abnormalities. In cases of anal cancer, the DRE may be repeated after diagnosis to evaluate the extent of the disease. Furthermore, for patients who have undergone treatment for lymph node recurrence without abdominoperineal resection (APR), the exam is recommended at regular intervals—every 3 to 6 months for a period of 5 years following treatment—to monitor for any signs of recurrence or complications. This follow-up protocol underscores the exam's importance in ongoing surveillance and management of cancer-related conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-081&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-082&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-083&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-084&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-085&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-089&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-186&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-187&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-192</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683079</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
