    <node id="Cancer Staging">
      <data key="d0">Cancer Staging</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A way to describe the extent of cancer at the time of diagnosis, used to reflect prognosis and guide treatment decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer staging is a process to describe the extent of cancer in the body, including tumor size, lymph node involvement, and metastasis, used to guide treatment and predict prognosis.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of determining the size, location, and spread of cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-106&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-157</data>
