    <node id="Epstein-Barr Virus">
      <data key="d0">Epstein-Barr Virus</data>
      <data key="d1">creature</data>
      <data key="d2">A common virus that causes mononucleosis and remains dormant in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;A virus associated with nasopharyngeal carcinoma, tested via DNA testing.&lt;SEP&gt;A common virus that causes infectious mononucleosis and is associated with certain cancers, including nasopharyngeal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Epstein-Barr virus (EBV) is a virus that can be present in the blood and is used in prognostic staging for nasopharyngeal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A virus that can be present in neck lymph nodes, associated with nasopharyngeal carcinoma.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-112&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-127&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-130&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-131&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-132</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683082</data>
