    <node id="Primary CNS Lymphoma">
      <data key="d0">Primary CNS Lymphoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Primary CNS Lymphoma is a rare and aggressive cancer that originates in lymphocytes within the central nervous system (CNS). It most commonly affects the brain, often developing deep within brain tissue, but can also occur in the spinal cord, cerebrospinal fluid, and the eyes. The disease can spread within the nervous system but rarely metastasizes to other areas of the body. Diagnosis typically requires a biopsy and imaging tests to confirm the presence of the malignancy.

As a specific type of lymphoma confined to the CNS, it is the subject of various therapeutic approaches discussed in medical literature. Treatment options for this condition are actively explored, with multiple therapies being considered or applied to manage the disease. The cancer's aggressive nature and its location within the CNS make it a challenging condition to treat, necessitating specialized medical intervention.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-111&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-112&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-113&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-114&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-115&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-117&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-118&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-119&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-120&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-121</data>
