    <node id="Fertility-Sparing Treatment">
      <data key="d0">Fertility-Sparing Treatment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Treatment options that aim to preserve the ability to become pregnant in the future, typically for small, early-stage cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;Treatment options that preserve fertility, such as trachelectomy.&lt;SEP&gt;Surgical approach that does not remove the uterus or ovaries, allowing for future natural pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Surgical treatment that preserves fertility, such as trachelectomy.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-135&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-140&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-141&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-143</data>
