    <node id="Thyroid Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Thyroid Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of cancer that forms in the thyroid gland, with several types, most curable with appropriate treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer that forms in the thyroid gland, with several types including papillary, follicular, oncocytic, medullary, and anaplastic.&lt;SEP&gt;A disease characterized by malignant cells in the thyroid gland, with different types including differentiated, medullary, and anaplastic.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cancer that affects the thyroid gland. Targeted therapies are used for certain thyroid cancers that cannot be treated with surgery or RAI therapy, have returned, or have metastasized.&lt;SEP&gt;A cancer that forms in the tissues of the thyroid gland.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cancer that affects the thyroid gland, with metastatic forms that may require targeted therapy or monitoring.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-146&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-147&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-148&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-149&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-150&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-153</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683087</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Thyroid Nodule">
      <data key="d0">Thyroid Nodule</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Small, often round areas of abnormal growth within the thyroid gland, most are benign and often asymptomatic.&lt;SEP&gt;A lump or abnormal growth in the thyroid gland that may be benign or cancerous.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-146&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-147</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683087</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Thyroid-Stimulating Hormone">
      <data key="d0">Thyroid-Stimulating Hormone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A hormone made by the pituitary gland that controls thyroid hormone production; blood test used to evaluate thyroid nodules.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-146</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683087</data>
