    <node id="Cutaneous B-Cell Lymphoma">
      <data key="d0">Cutaneous B-Cell Lymphoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of lymphoma that starts in B cells and appears on the skin.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of primary cutaneous lymphoma that develops from abnormal B cells, often appearing as nodules under the skin that may look like small pimples called papules.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cancer that affects B-cells in the skin, requiring accurate testing for diagnosis and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-171&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-172&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-173</data>
