    </node>
    <node id="External Beam Radiation Therapy (EBRT)">
      <data key="d0">External Beam Radiation Therapy (EBRT)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">External Beam Radiation Therapy (EBRT) is a form of cancer treatment that delivers high-energy radiation beams—such as x-rays or particles—from a machine positioned outside the patient's body. This technique aims the radiation precisely at the tumor or cancerous area from an external source, distinguishing it from internal radiation methods. EBRT is utilized across various treatment scenarios to destroy cancer cells or shrink tumors by damaging their DNA, thereby inhibiting their ability to grow and divide. The therapy encompasses advanced delivery techniques, including Intensity-Modulated Radiation Therapy (IMRT), which allows for more precise dose distribution to the tumor while sparing surrounding healthy tissue. As a non-invasive approach, EBRT is typically administered in multiple sessions, with the treatment plan tailored to the specific type, location, and stage of cancer. Its objective is to target malignant cells effectively while minimizing damage to adjacent normal structures, making it a cornerstone of oncological care for both curative and palliative purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-135&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-141&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-142&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-144&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-148&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-150&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-183&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-189</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Urothelium">
      <data key="d0">Urothelium</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The inner lining of the bladder that prevents urine from leaking back into the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The inner layer of the urinary tract, including the bladder, kidneys, ureters, and urethra. Cancer of the urothelium can start in these areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-173&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-174</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Urinary Tract">
      <data key="d0">Urinary Tract</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The system of organs including kidneys, ureters, bladder, and urethra that produce and excrete urine.&lt;SEP&gt;The system in the body that produces and excretes urine, including the kidneys, ureters, bladder, and urethra.&lt;SEP&gt;The system including kidneys, ureters, bladder, and urethra, where cancer may be located.&lt;SEP&gt;The system including kidneys, ureters, bladder, and urethra, examined in various procedures.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-173&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-174&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-176&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-177</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Urothelial Cells">
      <data key="d0">Urothelial Cells</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Stretchy cells lining the inside of the bladder and the rest of the urinary tract.&lt;SEP&gt;Cells that make up the inner lining of the bladder, where most bladder cancers start.&lt;SEP&gt;Cells that make up the inner lining of the bladder, where most bladder cancers originate.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-173&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-179&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-180</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1788683089</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Small Cell Carcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Small Cell Carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A less common type of bladder cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A non-urothelial type of bladder cancer that is less common.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-173&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-174</data>
