    <node id="Perianal Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Perianal Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A type of anal cancer that starts in the perianal region, with stages I-III being non-metastatic.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer that occurs in the perianal area, stages I-III are nonmetastatic.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of cancer occurring in the perianal area, with grades and treatment options described.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer that occurs in the perianal area, for which local excision may be an option in some cases.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-189&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-190&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-191&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-194</data>
