      <data key="d7">9.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relation (Care Team, Primary Care Physician) describes the role and involvement of a primary care physician within a patient’s care team. The primary care physician is consistently identified as an integral member of the care team, actively participating in the patient’s overall care. Beyond mere membership, this physician is considered a partner in the patient’s care, indicating a collaborative and engaged role in medical decision-making and treatment planning.

A key responsibility associated with this relation is communication. The primary care physician must be kept informed and updated on any changes relevant to the patient’s care. Specifically, the physician should be notified of any modifications to the care team contact list, ensuring they have current and accurate information for coordination. This requirement for ongoing updates underscores the physician’s need to stay current with the team’s structure and any evolving care circumstances. Overall, the relation emphasizes both the physician’s foundational presence on the team and the necessity of continuous, transparent communication to support effective, coordinated patient care.</data>
      <data key="d9">care,communication,coordination,informed,member,member of,part of,partnership,update,updates</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-066&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-095&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-161&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-163&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-173</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1788683094</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
