    <edge source="Imaging Tests" target="Radiologist">
      <data key="d7">12.0</data>
      <data key="d8">(Imaging Tests, Radiologist) is a professional relationship in healthcare wherein a radiologist is responsible for interpreting imaging tests. This process involves a radiologist examining or studying the images produced by these tests, such as X-rays, MRIs, or CT scans, to analyze the results. Following the interpretation, the radiologist writes a detailed report of their findings. This report is then communicated to the referring doctor or physician, and more broadly, to the patient's care team or other health care providers. The radiologist's role is thus to serve as a diagnostic expert who translates imaging data into actionable medical information for the clinicians responsible for patient treatment.</data>
      <data key="d9">expertise,interpretation,interpreted by,interprets,reads,report,reporting,reports</data>
      <data key="d10">doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-052&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-071&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-082&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-090&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-101&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-128&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3d7a4f05339f0e3f3870b407d21d9c8a-chunk-155</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1788683096</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
    <edge source="Imaging Tests" target="NCCN Guidelines for Patients® Adrenal Tumors, 2022">
